        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">
            <link address="#BridgeGeometry_3Beam">Archive - 3-Beam Geometry</link>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">
            <link address="#PedBridgeWeights_3Beams">Archive - 3-Beam Weights</link>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">
            <link address="#VoidPedBridge">Archive - Previous Ped Bridge</link>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">Revision: 8 October 2026, coherence responses. End-bent input uses loaded nodes 15 and 34, 103-in bearing spacing and a 42-in-wide by 36-in-deep cap. Both end bents follow the controlling configuration. End-bent pedestals are 30 in long; pier pedestals remain 48 in. Deferred wall quantities and remaining design checks are identified in the current record.</paragraph>
        <section name="PierJournalRevision20261009" capture="False" hide="false">
            <heading level="1" keepwithnext="True">Pier revision — responses applied, 9 October 2026</heading>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Current pier geometry and source references use the replacement Pier_Fixed report. The shared cap length and gross direct-pier wind width are both 230 in; gross cap volume remains 230 ft³ and pier pedestals remain 48 in. The matching raw XML is still needed to verify the offset correction. The former C005 (removed 19 October 2026) was left unchanged in that revision and reinforcement remains separate. Completed Excel responses and source snapshots are archived under tasks/T006/sources.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">
                <link address="#BridgeGeometry_2Beam.PierCurrentGeometry">Current pier cap geometry</link>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">
                <link address="#FBMPPier.PierSourceModelRecord">Current report source</link>
            </paragraph>
        </section>
    </report>
