        <section name="NotebookGeometryUpdate20260929" capture="False" hide="false">
            <heading>Coordinated notebook geometry — 29 September 2026</heading>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Current project basis: Bridge_Geo_2_Beam_Reorganized, intersecting-tangent profile, centered two-beam crowned deck, zero beam raises and parabolic span cambers. The normal slab area excludes all haunch concrete. Haunches are calculated and counted separately. This journal form reproduces that selected notebook mode; changing notebook profile or deck mode requires a coordinated update.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pier_pile_count = 4" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Pier_pile_count = 4</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Number of equally spaced piles in the transverse row.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pier_pile_diameter = 20 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Pier_pile_diameter = 20 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Nominal pile outside diameter selected by the user.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pier_pile_spacingRatio = 3" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Pier_pile_spacingRatio = 3</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Pile center spacing expressed as a multiple of the pile diameter.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PierCap_endClear = 15 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>PierCap_endClear = 15 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Nominal geometric distance from the outside face of each end pile to the cap end. No additional tolerance is added to this entered 15-in dimension.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PierCap_length = (Pier_pile_count-1)*Pile_spacing+Pier_pile_diameter+2*PierCap_endClear to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>PierCap_length = (Pier_pile_count-1)*Pile_spacing+Pier_pile_diameter+2*PierCap_endClear to ft in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 19 ft 2 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Three 5-ft pile spaces plus one 20-in diameter plus two 15-in end clearances = 19 ft 2 in.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PGL_start_elev = 47.661 ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>PGL_start_elev = 47.661 ft</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Notebook alignment elevation at begin bridge, station 15+93.22.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PGL_end_elev = 47.673 ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>PGL_end_elev = 47.673 ft</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Notebook alignment elevation at end bridge, station 18+05.47.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PGL_nominalGrade = 0.005" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>PGL_nominalGrade = 0.005</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Balanced intersecting-tangent profile uses the existing nominal 0.5% grade.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PGL_pier_elev = (PGL_start_elev+PGL_nominalGrade*Span_1+PGL_end_elev+PGL_nominalGrade*Span_2)/2 to ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>PGL_pier_elev = (PGL_start_elev+PGL_nominalGrade*Span_1+PGL_end_elev+PGL_nominalGrade*Span_2)/2 to ft</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 48.198 ft</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Notebook balanced profile intersection at the idealized pier support.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Deck_crossfall = 0.02" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Deck_crossfall = 0.02</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Magnitude of the 2% crown slope on each side of the alignment.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Beam_topFlange_width = 48 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Beam_topFlange_width = 48 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Width integrated for each beam haunch in the notebook.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Beam_camber_1 = 0.124592744006574 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Beam_camber_1 = 0.124592744006574 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Upward parabolic camber in span 1, zero at idealized supports. Net camber at 120 days, Mathcad NetCamber for span 1; notebook CONFIG spans[0].camber_in.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Beam_camber_2 = 0.5671714630550072 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Beam_camber_2 = 0.5671714630550072 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Upward parabolic camber in span 2, zero at idealized supports. Net camber at 120 days, Mathcad NetCamber for span 2; notebook CONFIG spans[1].camber_in.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Haunch_min = 0.5 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Haunch_min = 0.5 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Minimum haunch at the controlling flange edge.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Beam_support_drop = Thickness_slab_peak+Beam_depth+Deck_crossfall*(Beam_spacing/2+Beam_topFlange_width/2)+Haunch_min+Max(Beam_camber_1,Beam_camber_2) to ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Beam_support_drop = Thickness_slab_peak+Beam_depth+Deck_crossfall*(Beam_spacing/2+Beam_topFlange_width/2)+Haunch_min+Max(Beam_camber_1,Beam_camber_2) to ft</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 3.715 ft</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Common downward offset from the profile support chord. Valid for the selected centered crowned section and tangent profiles within each span. Equals the notebook common support drop 3.7148 ft (model e9b41b8eaf) with the notebook net cambers.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Beam_bottom_start = PGL_start_elev-Beam_support_drop to ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Beam_bottom_start = PGL_start_elev-Beam_support_drop to ft</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 43.946 ft</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Beam soffit at the idealized begin-bridge support.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Beam_bottom_pier = PGL_pier_elev-Beam_support_drop to ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Beam_bottom_pier = PGL_pier_elev-Beam_support_drop to ft</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 44.483 ft</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Beam soffit at the idealized common pier support.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Beam_bottom_end = PGL_end_elev-Beam_support_drop to ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Beam_bottom_end = PGL_end_elev-Beam_support_drop to ft</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 43.958 ft</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Beam soffit at the idealized end-bridge support.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Deck_area = Deck_out2out*Thickness_slab_peak to ft^2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Deck_area = Deck_out2out*Thickness_slab_peak to ft^2</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 6.792 ft^2</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Normal slab-only area: 13 ft 7 in multiplied by 6 in = 6.7916667 ft². No haunch or local end-thickening volume is embedded in this area.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Haunch_average_1 = Haunch_min+Max(Beam_camber_1,Beam_camber_2)-2*Beam_camber_1/3+Deck_crossfall*Beam_topFlange_width/2 to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Haunch_average_1 = Haunch_min+Max(Beam_camber_1,Beam_camber_2)-2*Beam_camber_1/3+Deck_crossfall*Beam_topFlange_width/2 to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 1.464 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Mean centerline haunch in span 1; integrates the parabolic camber and symmetric flange crossfall exactly.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Haunch_average_2 = Haunch_min+Max(Beam_camber_1,Beam_camber_2)-2*Beam_camber_2/3+Deck_crossfall*Beam_topFlange_width/2 to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Haunch_average_2 = Haunch_min+Max(Beam_camber_1,Beam_camber_2)-2*Beam_camber_2/3+Deck_crossfall*Beam_topFlange_width/2 to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 1.169 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Mean centerline haunch in span 2.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Haunch_volume_span1 = Beam_count*Span_1*Beam_topFlange_width*Haunch_average_1 to ft^3" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Haunch_volume_span1 = Beam_count*Span_1*Beam_topFlange_width*Haunch_average_1 to ft^3</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 104.781 ft^3</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Both beam haunches over full span 1.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Haunch_volume_span2 = Beam_count*Span_2*Beam_topFlange_width*Haunch_average_2 to ft^3" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Haunch_volume_span2 = Beam_count*Span_2*Beam_topFlange_width*Haunch_average_2 to ft^3</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 81.756 ft^3</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Both beam haunches over full span 2.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Haunch_totalVolume = Haunch_volume_span1+Haunch_volume_span2 to ft^3" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Haunch_totalVolume = Haunch_volume_span1+Haunch_volume_span2 to ft^3</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 186.538 ft^3</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Full bridge haunch volume, 185.8366667 ft³ at the selected notebook inputs. The pier tributary takes half once; do not multiply by beam count again.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Haunch_volume_perBeam = Haunch_totalVolume/Beam_count to ft^3" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Haunch_volume_perBeam = Haunch_totalVolume/Beam_count to ft^3</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 93.269 ft^3</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Full bridge haunch volume for each identical transverse beam line.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="2" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Check_notebook_quantity = If(And(Beam_count == 2, Abs(Deck_area-6.79166666666667 ft^2)&lt;0.000001 ft^2, Abs(Haunch_totalVolume-185.836666666667 ft^3)&lt;0.000001 ft^3), &quot;MATCHES 2026-09-29 NOTEBOOK&quot;, &quot;INPUTS CHANGED - RECONCILE NOTEBOOK&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Check_notebook_quantity = If(And(Beam_count == 2, Abs(Deck_area-6.79166666666667 ft^2)&lt;0.000001 ft^2, Abs(Haunch_totalVolume-185.836666666667 ft^3)&lt;0.000001 ft^3), "MATCHES 2026-09-29 NOTEBOOK", "INPUTS CHANGED - RECONCILE NOTEBOOK")</expbody>
                    <expresult> = INPUTS CHANGED - RECONCILE NOTEBOOK</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Snapshot reconciliation check. Future input changes retain live formulas and request reconciliation rather than silently showing the old check.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Bearing stations: the notebook retains the common idealized support at 17+00.57. Physical pier bearing rows are 10.5 in either side of pier CL. Confirm end-bearing station datums and individual seat grades before using these elevations for setting out.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Local thickened deck ends remain a separate unresolved detail and quantity. Existing analysis force exports predate the revised 36-in cap and revised deck dead load; regenerate the structural analysis forces before final use of the pier cap design (CapDesignPier).</paragraph>
        </section>
        <float />
        <stylerule applytoall="True" type="Any" leftindent="0.25 in" spacingafter="4" />
        <stylerule type="AnyEquation" name="Required Input" texthighlight="#F7E6B9" />
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontweight="bold" fontsize="16" fontunderline="True" textdecoration="underline" horzalign="Center" spacingafter="12">BRIDGE GEOMETRY</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7" background="#FFF8E9" fontweight="bold">GEOMETRY BASIS — Type F pads, 6-in pedestals and a single 36-in cap-depth input define the support stack. Use the notebook pier beam soffit and derive cap elevations, wind arms and terrain-relative heights. Verify the individual seat grades, any separate plates, retained concrete wind envelope, terrain reference and gross pier-face width against the final pier section.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">WIDTH BASIS — The DXF labels 12 ft between the inside parapet faces. Handrail projections are deducted separately to determine the unobstructed walking width.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="12">Central geometry module. Bridge dimensions used by wind, ADA, and FB-MultiPier calculations are defined here and referenced live by the other modules.</paragraph>
        <heading leftindent="0.25 in" spacingafter="4">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="heading">1.</paragraphlabel>
            General Bridge Layout
        </heading>
        <paragraph />
        <paragraph level="1">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">1.</paragraphlabel>
            <image source="Resource32" width="389.61827578102765" height="88.94084351407847" />
             RFQ
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph level="1">
            <image source="Resource33" width="434.04761872191796" height="47.70401236970878" />
            RFQ
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">2.</paragraphlabel>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph level="1">
            <image source="Resource34" />
            RFQ
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">3.</paragraphlabel>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph level="1">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">4.</paragraphlabel>
            <image source="Resource35" width="561.2621667885422" height="52.14306581777427" />
            RFQ
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph level="1">
            <image source="Resource36" width="567.6132056408824" height="62.00196264477785" />
            RFQ
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">5.</paragraphlabel>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph level="1">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">6.</paragraphlabel>
            <image source="Resource37" width="558.8869651906622" height="25.2400564924815" />
            RFQ
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph level="1">
            <image source="Resource38" width="562.4664476709593" height="56.609526346238425" />
            RFQ
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">7.</paragraphlabel>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph level="1">
            <image source="Resource40" width="286.59880620265596" height="44.14436588429538" />
            <image source="Resource39" />
            From A08 Typ Sections Sheet 11
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">8.</paragraphlabel>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">9.</paragraphlabel>
            <dynexp formula="BeginBridge_station=1593.22">
                <expbody>BeginBridge_station=1593.22</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Position along the project alignment at the beginning of the bridge.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_001_BeginBridge_station" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This is an alignment station stored as a numerical input. A station locates a point along the bridge route; it is not a vertical elevation. The span lengths below now follow differences of the notebook station inputs.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="CLPier_station = 1700.57">
                <expbody>CLPier_station = 1700.57</expbody>
            </dynexp>
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">10.</paragraphlabel>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Position along the project alignment at the centerline of the intermediate pier.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_002_CLPier_station" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This is an alignment station stored as a numerical input. A station locates a point along the bridge route; it is not a vertical elevation. The span lengths below now follow differences of the notebook station inputs.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">11.</paragraphlabel>
            <dynexp formula="EndBridge_station = 1805.47">
                <expbody>EndBridge_station = 1805.47</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Position along the project alignment at the end of the bridge.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_003_EndBridge_station" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This is an alignment station stored as a numerical input. A station locates a point along the bridge route; it is not a vertical elevation. The span lengths below now follow differences of the notebook station inputs.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Span_1 = (CLPier_station-BeginBridge_station)*1 ft">
                <expbody>Span_1 = (CLPier_station-BeginBridge_station)*1 ft</expbody>
                <expresult> = 107.35 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">12.</paragraphlabel>
            <dynexp formula="Span_1 to ft">
                <expbody>Span_1 to ft</expbody>
                <expresult> = 107.35 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Notebook station-derived length of the span between the beginning of the bridge and the intermediate pier.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_004_Span_1" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This length supplies the bridge geometry and its share of loads delivered to the intermediate pier. The second displayed expression converts the same entered feet-and-inches length to decimal feet; it does not define another span.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Span_2 = (EndBridge_station-CLPier_station)*1 ft">
                <expbody>Span_2 = (EndBridge_station-CLPier_station)*1 ft</expbody>
                <expresult> = 104.9 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
            <dynexp formula="Span_2 to ft">
                <expbody>Span_2 to ft</expbody>
                <expresult> = 104.9 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">13.</paragraphlabel>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Notebook station-derived length of the span between the intermediate pier and the end of the bridge.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_005_Span_2" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This length supplies the bridge geometry and its share of loads delivered to the intermediate pier. The second displayed expression converts the same entered feet-and-inches length to decimal feet; it does not define another span.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">14.</paragraphlabel>
            <dynexp formula="TotalSpan=Span_1+Span_2">
                <expbody>TotalSpan=Span_1+Span_2</expbody>
                <expresult> = 212.25 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Combined length of the two bridge spans.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_006_TotalSpan" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                Add 
                <dynexp formula="Span_1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Span_1</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the first span, to 
                <dynexp formula="Span_2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Span_2</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the second span. This gives the full length represented by the two-span model. Half of this sum is used as the intermediate pier’s contributing length for uniform loads on simply supported spans.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="PierCap_width=4ft">
                <expbody>PierCap_width=4ft</expbody>
            </dynexp>
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">15.</paragraphlabel>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Width of the pier cap used as the narrow projected wind dimension.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_007_PierCap_width" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This entered width is multiplied by the adopted exposed wall-and-cap height to form the rectangular area for direct transverse pier wind. It is a horizontal dimension, not the cap depth or the length of the cap across all piles.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">16.</paragraphlabel>
            <dynexp formula="PierCap_ht = 36 in to ft in" style="Required Input">
                <expbody>PierCap_ht = 36 in to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 3 ft 0 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Single authoritative pier-cap vertical depth.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_008_PierCap_ht" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">Full top-to-bottom cap depth. Every current two-beam cap datum and cap-volume calculation references this input. The archived three-beam module is a separate configuration.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">17.</paragraphlabel>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph level="1">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="paragraph">18.</paragraphlabel>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph level="1">
            <image source="Resource19" width="204.19660148800085" height="193.39394257057117" />
            <image source="Resource20" width="193.82571573214696" height="186.45191132929352" />
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph level="1" />
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="3' 2 1/2&quot; + 3 1/4&quot; - 3'">
                <expbody>3' 2 1/2" + 3 1/4" - 3'</expbody>
                <expresult> = 0 ft 5 3/4 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Remaining vertical dimension in the FIB36 shear-bar embedment note.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_009_3_2_1_2_3_1_4_3" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">Add the entered 3 ft 2-1/2 in dimension and the 3-1/4 in allowance, then subtract the 3 ft beam-depth term. The result is the remaining distance in this geometry chain. This arithmetic note does not itself show a reinforcing-bar development-length or capacity check.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <heading>
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="heading">2.</paragraphlabel>
            Superstructure Elevations
        </heading>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="TO_Slab = PGL_pier_elev to ft">
                <expbody>TO_Slab = PGL_pier_elev to ft</expbody>
                <expresult> = 48.198 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Notebook PGL slab-crown elevation at the idealized pier station.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_010_TO_Slab" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This is a vertical project elevation, measured from the project datum. It locates the slab surface in space. It is not the slab thickness, the slab height above nearby ground, or an alignment station.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="BO_LowBeam = Beam_bottom_pier to ft">
                <expbody>BO_LowBeam = Beam_bottom_pier to ft</expbody>
                <expresult> = 44.483 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Elevation of the bottom of the low beam.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_011_BO_LowBeam" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                Start at 
                <dynexp formula="TO_Slab" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>TO_Slab</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the top-of-slab elevation. Subtract the entered 3.71 ft vertical distance from the slab top down to the low beam bottom. Subtraction moves the point downward while keeping the same elevation datum.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <section name="G2PriorImage_Resource25" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7" fontweight="bold">PRIOR GEOMETRY — retained for reference; this image does not define the current two-beam section.</paragraph>
            <paragraph>
                <image source="Resource25" width="265.13047365339094" height="146.03908056973728" />
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <heading level="1">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="heading">2.1.</paragraphlabel>
            Vertical Clearance
        </heading>
        <section name="G2PriorImage_Resource49" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7" fontweight="bold">PRIOR GEOMETRY — retained for reference; this image does not define the current two-beam section.</paragraph>
            <paragraph>
                <image source="Resource49" width="598.7224801851722" height="258.80262046713847" />
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <heading level="1">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="heading">2.2.</paragraphlabel>
            Cross Sections
        </heading>
        <heading level="2">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="heading">2.2.1.</paragraphlabel>
            Begin Bridge
        </heading>
        <paragraph>
            <dynexp formula="BeginBridge_station">
                <expbody>BeginBridge_station</expbody>
                <expresult> = 1593.22</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <section name="G2PriorImage_Resource153" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7" fontweight="bold">PRIOR GEOMETRY — retained for reference; this image does not define the current two-beam section.</paragraph>
            <paragraph>
                <image source="Resource153" />
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <heading level="2">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="heading">2.2.2.</paragraphlabel>
            CL Pier
        </heading>
        <paragraph>
            <dynexp formula="CLPier_station">
                <expbody>CLPier_station</expbody>
                <expresult> = 1700.57</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <section name="G2PriorImage_Resource154" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7" fontweight="bold">PRIOR GEOMETRY — retained for reference; this image does not define the current two-beam section.</paragraph>
            <paragraph>
                <image source="Resource154" />
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <heading level="2">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="heading">2.2.3.</paragraphlabel>
            End Bridge
        </heading>
        <paragraph>
            <dynexp formula="EndBridge_station">
                <expbody>EndBridge_station</expbody>
                <expresult> = 1805.47</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <section name="G2PriorImage_Resource155" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7" fontweight="bold">PRIOR GEOMETRY — retained for reference; this image does not define the current two-beam section.</paragraph>
            <paragraph>
                <image source="Resource155" />
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <heading>
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="heading">3.</paragraphlabel>
            Bridge Cross-Section Widths
        </heading>
        <embed spacingbefore="8" spacingafter="12">
            <canvas name="G2UpdatedSection" title="Two-beam section dimensions" unit="in" size="6.5 in; 4.8 in; scaletofit">
                <include target="Library.Geometry" />
                <planecontainer origin="0.15, 4.57, 0" dir="1, 0, 0" normal="0, 0, 1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Two-beam section — dimensioned superstructure</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="0.15, 0.14, 0" dir="1, 0, 0" normal="0, 0, 1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#727B84"><textvalue>SCHEMATIC — NOT TO SCALE; cap and ground geometry require confirmation.</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lines pts="1.35000, 1.50000, 0; 5.15000, 1.50000, 0; 5.15000, 1.65000, 0; 3.25000, 1.73000, 0; 1.35000, 1.65000, 0; 1.35000, 1.50000, 0" linecolor="#29333D" linepattern="Solid" linethickness="1" />
                <lines pts="1.60000, 1.50000, 0; 2.52000, 1.50000, 0; 2.52000, 1.36000, 0; 2.19000, 1.26000, 0; 2.19000, 0.98000, 0; 2.43000, 0.91000, 0; 2.43000, 0.77000, 0; 1.69000, 0.77000, 0; 1.69000, 0.91000, 0; 1.93000, 0.98000, 0; 1.93000, 1.26000, 0; 1.60000, 1.36000, 0; 1.60000, 1.50000, 0" linecolor="#29333D" linepattern="Solid" linethickness="1" />
                <lines pts="3.98000, 1.50000, 0; 4.90000, 1.50000, 0; 4.90000, 1.36000, 0; 4.57000, 1.26000, 0; 4.57000, 0.98000, 0; 4.81000, 0.91000, 0; 4.81000, 0.77000, 0; 4.07000, 0.77000, 0; 4.07000, 0.91000, 0; 4.31000, 0.98000, 0; 4.31000, 1.26000, 0; 3.98000, 1.36000, 0; 3.98000, 1.50000, 0" linecolor="#29333D" linepattern="Solid" linethickness="1" />
                <lines pts="1.40000, 1.65000, 0; 1.62000, 1.65000, 0; 1.62000, 2.28000, 0; 1.40000, 2.28000, 0; 1.40000, 1.65000, 0" linecolor="#29333D" linepattern="Solid" linethickness="1" />
                <lines pts="4.88000, 1.65000, 0; 5.10000, 1.65000, 0; 5.10000, 2.28000, 0; 4.88000, 2.28000, 0; 4.88000, 1.65000, 0" linecolor="#29333D" linepattern="Solid" linethickness="1" />
                <lines pts="1.51000, 2.28000, 0; 1.51000, 2.88000, 0" linecolor="#29333D" linepattern="Solid" linethickness="1" />
                <lines pts="4.99000, 2.28000, 0; 4.99000, 2.88000, 0" linecolor="#29333D" linepattern="Solid" linethickness="1" />
                <lines pts="4.99000, 2.88000, 0; 4.98790, 2.93888, 0; 4.98162, 2.99762, 0; 4.97117, 3.05608, 0; 4.95657, 3.11411, 0; 4.93785, 3.17158, 0; 4.91508, 3.22834, 0; 4.88829, 3.28427, 0; 4.85755, 3.33922, 0; 4.82294, 3.39307, 0; 4.78454, 3.44568, 0; 4.74245, 3.49692, 0; 4.69676, 3.54668, 0; 4.64758, 3.59484, 0; 4.59504, 3.64127, 0; 4.53925, 3.68587, 0; 4.48037, 3.72853, 0; 4.41851, 3.76914, 0; 4.35384, 3.80761, 0; 4.28652, 3.84385, 0; 4.21669, 3.87776, 0; 4.14454, 3.90927, 0; 4.07023, 3.93831, 0; 3.99395, 3.96479, 0; 3.91587, 3.98866, 0; 3.83619, 4.00985, 0; 3.75510, 4.02833, 0; 3.67279, 4.04404, 0; 3.58946, 4.05694, 0; 3.50531, 4.06701, 0; 3.42055, 4.07422, 0; 3.33538, 4.07855, 0; 3.25000, 4.08000, 0; 3.16462, 4.07855, 0; 3.07945, 4.07422, 0; 2.99469, 4.06701, 0; 2.91054, 4.05694, 0; 2.82721, 4.04404, 0; 2.74490, 4.02833, 0; 2.66381, 4.00985, 0; 2.58413, 3.98866, 0; 2.50605, 3.96479, 0; 2.42977, 3.93831, 0; 2.35546, 3.90927, 0; 2.28331, 3.87776, 0; 2.21348, 3.84385, 0; 2.14616, 3.80761, 0; 2.08149, 3.76914, 0; 2.01963, 3.72853, 0; 1.96075, 3.68587, 0; 1.90496, 3.64127, 0; 1.85242, 3.59484, 0; 1.80324, 3.54668, 0; 1.75755, 3.49692, 0; 1.71546, 3.44568, 0; 1.67706, 3.39307, 0; 1.64245, 3.33922, 0; 1.61171, 3.28427, 0; 1.58492, 3.22834, 0; 1.56215, 3.17158, 0; 1.54343, 3.11411, 0; 1.52883, 3.05608, 0; 1.51838, 2.99762, 0; 1.51210, 2.93888, 0; 1.51000, 2.88000, 0" linecolor="#29333D" linepattern="Solid" linethickness="1" />
                <lines pts="1.51000, 2.88000, 0; 4.99000, 2.88000, 0" linecolor="#727B84" linepattern="Dashes" linethickness=".6" />
                <lineardim startpoint="1.62, 2.28, 0" endpoint="4.88, 2.28, 0" pointondimline="3.25, 2.49, 0" formula="BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Dist_insideParapets" linecolor="#1766A0" textcolor="#1766A0" linethickness="0.7" fontsize="9"><num>12 ft</num></lineardim>
                <lineardim startpoint="1.35, 1.5, 0" endpoint="5.15, 1.5, 0" pointondimline="3.25, 0.46, 0" formula="BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Deck_out2out" linecolor="#1766A0" textcolor="#1766A0" linethickness="0.7" fontsize="9"><num>13 ft 7 in</num></lineardim>
                <lineardim startpoint="2.06, 0.77, 0" endpoint="4.44, 0.77, 0" pointondimline="3.25, 1.07, 0" formula="BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Beam_spacing" linecolor="#1766A0" textcolor="#1766A0" linethickness="0.7" fontsize="9"><num>8 ft 7 in</num></lineardim>
                <lineardim startpoint="4.99, 2.28, 0" endpoint="4.99, 4.08, 0" pointondimline="5.66, 3.2, 0" formula="BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Fence_ht" linecolor="#1766A0" textcolor="#1766A0" linethickness="0.7" fontsize="9"><num>9 ft 8 5/16 in</num></lineardim>
                <planecontainer origin="5.44, 4.21, 0" dir="1, 0, 0" normal="0, 0, 1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#1766A0"><textvalue>Gross fence</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="2.55, 3.02, 0" dir="1, 0, 0" normal="0, 0, 1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#727B84"><textvalue>Post centerline spacing</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lineardim startpoint="1.51, 2.88, 0" endpoint="4.99, 2.88, 0" pointondimline="3.25, 3.33, 0" formula="BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Fence_postSpacing" linecolor="#1766A0" textcolor="#1766A0" linethickness="0.7" fontsize="9"><num>12 ft 8 in</num></lineardim>
                <planecontainer origin="0.24, 1.12, 0" dir="1, 0, 0" normal="0, 0, 1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Two FIB36</textvalue></planecontainer>
            </canvas>
        </embed>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Beam_count = 2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                <expbody>Beam_count = 2</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Number of longitudinal beams.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Beam_count" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Two-beam configuration specified for the revised bridge. The DXF contains two FIB36 section definitions.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Beam_spacing = 8 ft 7 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                <expbody>Beam_spacing = 8 ft 7 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Center-to-center spacing of the two beams.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Beam_spacing" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Pier.dxf dimension *D5374: 8 ft 7 in; corroborated by the two half-spacing dimensions.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Beam_depth = 3 ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                <expbody>Beam_depth = 3 ft</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">FIB36 nominal beam depth.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Beam_depth" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">The two Beam-FI-36 block definitions in Pier.dxf have a 3 ft depth. Their placement and soffit elevations are not included in model space.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Parapet_ht = 42 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                <expbody>Parapet_ht = 42 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Parapet height above its deck support surface.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Parapet_ht" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Pier.dxf dimension *D5377: 3 ft 6 in.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Bridge_clearWidth = 12 ft">
                <expbody>Bridge_clearWidth = 12 ft</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">DXF clear width between inside parapet faces.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_012_Bridge_clearWidth" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Pier.dxf dimension *D5384 is between the inside parapet faces. It is not a handrail-to-handrail clearance. The retained handrail projection is deducted in the separate walking-clearance expression.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Handrail_width = 3.5 in">
                <expbody>Handrail_width = 3.5 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Retained projection of one handrail — confirm with the railing detail.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_013_Handrail_width" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">The supplied pier dimension blocks do not establish the handrail projection. This previous input is retained only to show the resulting walking clearance; it does not increase the DXF deck width.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Dist_insideParapets = Bridge_clearWidth">
                <expbody>Dist_insideParapets = Bridge_clearWidth</expbody>
                <expresult> = 12 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Distance between inside parapet faces.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_014_Dist_insideParapets" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">The DXF clear-width dimension already terminates on the inside parapet faces. Do not add handrail projections to it.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Bridge_handrailClearWidth = Dist_insideParapets - 2*Handrail_width" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Bridge_handrailClearWidth = Dist_insideParapets - 2*Handrail_width</expbody>
                <expresult> = 11 ft 5 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Walking width clear of both handrail projections.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Bridge_handrailClearWidth" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Subtract the projection of one handrail on each side from the DXF parapet-face clearance. This result remains conditional on the retained handrail projection.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Parapet_width = 8 in">
                <expbody>Parapet_width = 8 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Full width of one parapet.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_015_Parapet_width" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Pier.dxf dimension *D5381: 8 in. The 6-1/2 in dimension *D5382 is at the chamfered portion, not the full parapet width.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Dist_outsideParapets = Dist_insideParapets+2*Parapet_width">
                <expbody>Dist_outsideParapets = Dist_insideParapets+2*Parapet_width</expbody>
                <expresult> = 13 ft 4 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Distance from the outside face of one parapet to the outside face of the other.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_016_Dist_outsideParapets" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                Add two times 
                <dynexp formula="Parapet_width" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Parapet_width</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , one parapet thickness on each side, to 
                <dynexp formula="Dist_insideParapets" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Dist_insideParapets</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the space between the inside faces. This includes both parapets but not the deck projection beyond them.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Distance_outFaceParapet_deckEdge = 1.5 in">
                <expbody>Distance_outFaceParapet_deckEdge = 1.5 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Deck projection outside one parapet.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_017_Distance_outFaceParapet_deckEdge" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">The 13 ft 7 in overall deck dimension (*D5380), 12 ft inside-face dimension (*D5384), and two 8 in parapets leave 3 in total for the two deck-edge projections. Use 1-1/2 in on each side.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Deck_out2out=Dist_outsideParapets+2*Distance_outFaceParapet_deckEdge">
                <expbody>Deck_out2out=Dist_outsideParapets+2*Distance_outFaceParapet_deckEdge</expbody>
                <expresult> = 13 ft 7 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Total width from one outside deck edge to the other.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_018_Deck_out2out" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                Start with 
                <dynexp formula="Dist_outsideParapets" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Dist_outsideParapets</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the outside-to-outside parapet distance. Add two times 
                <dynexp formula="Distance_outFaceParapet_deckEdge" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Distance_outFaceParapet_deckEdge</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , one deck-edge projection at each side. The sum includes the clear walking space, handrail allowances, both parapets, and both outer deck projections.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Deck_out2out/2">
                <expbody>Deck_out2out/2</expbody>
                <expresult> = 6 ft 9.5 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Distance from the deck centerline to one outside edge for a symmetric section.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_019_Deck_out2out_2" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                Divide 
                <dynexp formula="Deck_out2out" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Deck_out2out</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the full outside-to-outside deck width, by 2. This gives the half-width used to lay out one side from the centerline.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Dist_insideParapets/2">
                <expbody>Dist_insideParapets/2</expbody>
                <expresult> = 6 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Distance from the bridge centerline to one inside parapet face for a symmetric section.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_020_Dist_insideParapets_2" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">
                Divide 
                <dynexp formula="Dist_insideParapets" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showidentifier="False" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Dist_insideParapets</expbody>
                </dynexp>
                , the distance between inside parapet faces, by 2. The answer is the half-width to one inside face, before crossing the parapet or the deck-edge projection.
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <heading>
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="heading">4.</paragraphlabel>
            Wind-Exposure Geometry
        </heading>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Wind_clearHeight = CapTop_aboveTerrain + BearingPlane_aboveCap to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Wind_clearHeight = CapTop_aboveTerrain + BearingPlane_aboveCap to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 18 ft 11.478 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Adopted terrain-to-beam-soffit height for the wind envelope.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Wind_clearHeight" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">Derived from the common support stack and terrain datum. Confirm the terrain reference, individual seat grades and any separate bearing plates.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Dist_windSuperCG_CapCG = BearingPlane_CapCG + Depth_SuperStr/2 to ft in">
                <expbody>Dist_windSuperCG_CapCG = BearingPlane_CapCG + Depth_SuperStr/2 to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 5 ft 9.062 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Concrete wind centroid above the cap centroid.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_021_Dist_windSuperCG_CapCG" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">Half the adopted concrete wind depth above the bearing/beam-soffit plane. This arm follows cap depth and support buildup automatically; it is not an independent input.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Depth_SuperStr=7'1&quot;">
                <expbody>Depth_SuperStr=7'1"</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Vertical depth of concrete bridge surface included in the horizontal-wind area.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_022_Depth_SuperStr" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This input represents the concrete superstructure outline seen from the side. Multiply pressure by this depth to get force per foot along the bridge. Half this depth is the offset from its area midpoint to its top in the fence-base geometry.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <section name="G2PriorImage_Resource13" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7" fontweight="bold">PRIOR GEOMETRY — retained for reference; this image does not define the current two-beam section.</paragraph>
            <paragraph spacingafter="4">
                <image source="Resource13" width="282.51726024959396" height="274.63305763797825" />
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Fence_postSpacing = Dist_insideParapets + Parapet_width" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Fence_postSpacing = Dist_insideParapets + Parapet_width</expbody>
                <expresult> = 12 ft 8 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Spacing between fence-post centerlines.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Fence_postSpacing" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Posts are centered on the parapets. The resulting 12 ft 8 in spacing agrees with Pier.dxf dimension *D5383.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Fence_radius = Fence_postSpacing/2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Fence_radius = Fence_postSpacing/2</expbody>
                <expresult> = 6 ft 4 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Hoop radius at the post centerline.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Fence_radius" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Half the post-centerline spacing. This differs from the outer hoop radius used for the gross wind outline.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Fence_straight_ht = 3 ft 2 9/16 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                <expbody>Fence_straight_ht = 3 ft 2 9/16 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Straight fence height from parapet top to springline.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Fence_straight_ht" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Pier.dxf dimension *D5378: 3 ft 2-9/16 in. Use the stated drawing dimension; the exported definition points differ slightly from the rounded label.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Fence_radialAllowance = 1 3/4 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                <expbody>Fence_radialAllowance = 1 3/4 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Radial offset from the post centerline to the outer hoop surface.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Fence_radialAllowance" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">The dimensioned outer rise of 6 ft 5-3/4 in (*D5376) exceeds half the 12 ft 8 in post spacing (*D5383) by 1-3/4 in. This offset is inferred from those drawing dimensions.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Fence_outerRadius = Fence_radius + Fence_radialAllowance" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Fence_outerRadius = Fence_radius + Fence_radialAllowance</expbody>
                <expresult> = 6 ft 5 3/4 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Outer hoop rise from springline to crown.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Fence_outerRadius" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Add the radial allowance to the centerline radius. This reproduces the 6 ft 5-3/4 in DXF rise and allows the outer profile to follow later width changes.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Fence_crownAboveSlab_DXF = 13 ft 3/4 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                <expbody>Fence_crownAboveSlab_DXF = 13 ft 3/4 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Dimensioned fence crown above the deck crown.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Fence_crownAboveSlab_DXF" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Pier.dxf dimension *D5375. It is retained as an independent drawing check, not substituted for the fence height above the parapet.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Fence_ht = Fence_straight_ht + Fence_outerRadius">
                <expbody>Fence_ht = Fence_straight_ht + Fence_outerRadius</expbody>
                <expresult> = 9 ft 8 5/16 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Gross exposed fence height above the parapet.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_023_Fence_ht" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Add the dimensioned straight leg and outer hoop rise. The result follows the outside silhouette used by the existing global projected-area wind model. The centerline radius remains a separate geometry variable.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Fence_base_CapCG = BearingPlane_CapCG + Depth_SuperStr to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Fence_base_CapCG = BearingPlane_CapCG + Depth_SuperStr to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 9 ft 3.562 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Fence base above the cap centroid.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Fence_base_CapCG" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">Top of the adopted concrete wind envelope. Fence springline and centroid reference this same cap datum.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Fence_spring_CapCG = Fence_base_CapCG + Fence_straight_ht" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Fence_spring_CapCG = Fence_base_CapCG + Fence_straight_ht</expbody>
                <expresult> = 12 ft 6 1/8 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Fence springline above the retained cap reference.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Fence_spring_CapCG" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Add the dimensioned straight fence height to the fence-base moment arm.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Fence_CG_CapCG = Fence_base_CapCG + Fence_ht/2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Fence_CG_CapCG = Fence_base_CapCG + Fence_ht/2</expbody>
                <expresult> = 14 ft 1 23/32 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Centroid of the gross projected fence face above the retained cap reference.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Fence_CG_CapCG" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">The existing uniform horizontal projected-face model places the resultant at half the exposed fence height.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Pier_tributaryLength = PierTrib_1+PierTrib_2 to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Pier_tributaryLength = PierTrib_1+PierTrib_2 to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 106 ft 1.5 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Tributary bridge length delivered to the intermediate pier.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Pier_tributaryLength" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Half of each of the two retained simply supported span lengths.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Wind_exposureHeight = Wind_clearHeight + Depth_SuperStr + Fence_ht" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Wind_exposureHeight = Wind_clearHeight + Depth_SuperStr + Fence_ht</expbody>
                <expresult> = 35 ft 8 51/64 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Fence crown height used by the existing exposure model.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Wind_exposureHeight" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">The crown height combines the centralized clearance assumption, concrete exposed depth, and revised outer fence height. Ground clearance and concrete depth require verification.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Concrete_top_aboveGround = Wind_clearHeight + Depth_SuperStr" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Concrete_top_aboveGround = Wind_clearHeight + Depth_SuperStr</expbody>
                <expresult> = 26 ft 0.478 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Concrete superstructure top above the retained ground reference.</paragraph>
        <section name="G2Notes_Concrete_top_aboveGround" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Used by the existing simplified-wind qualification check. This remains provisional until the source geometry is confirmed.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="Pier_windFace_width = PierCap_length to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Pier_windFace_width = PierCap_length to in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 230 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Broad-face projected pier width — current cap length.</paragraph>
        <section name="CapDatumNote_Pier_windFace_width" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">Use the report cap length, 230 in, as the gross direct-pier wind width per coherence response 06. Width remains a live link to the shared cap geometry. Separate wall/fin concrete quantities retain their own dimensions.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Pier_wall_area = Pier_windFace_width*PierCap_ht_toTop to ft^2">
                <expbody>Pier_wall_area = Pier_windFace_width*PierCap_ht_toTop to ft^2</expbody>
                <expresult> = 349.656 ft^2</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Gross broad-face direct-pier wind area.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_024_Pier_wall_area" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">Gross rectangular projected width times the shared terrain-to-cap-top height. Both direct-pier wind directions use the same height datum.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="PierCap_ht_toTop = CapTop_aboveTerrain to ft in">
                <expbody>PierCap_ht_toTop = CapTop_aboveTerrain to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 18 ft 2.915 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Exposed wall-and-cap height for the adopted direct-pier wind rectangle.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_025_PierCap_ht_toTop" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">Uses the same terrain-to-cap-top chain as the superstructure wind geometry. This is the gross projected height, not cap depth or wall volume height.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <section name="G2PriorImage_Resource142" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7" fontweight="bold">PRIOR GEOMETRY — retained for reference; this image does not define the current two-beam section.</paragraph>
            <paragraph>
                <image source="Resource142" width="145.1302843016055" height="208.2304079109981" />
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph />
        <heading>
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="heading">5.</paragraphlabel>
            FBMP / Substructure Geometry
        </heading>
        <section name="G2PriorImage_Resource138" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7" fontweight="bold">PRIOR GEOMETRY — retained for reference; this image does not define the current two-beam section.</paragraph>
            <paragraph level="1">
                <image source="Resource138" width="221.81260524956744" height="230.38507308529825" />
                <image source="Resource12" width="217.06903990270285" height="142.14521000080367" />
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Distance_Algn2Terrain = TO_Slab-Terrain_elev to ft">
                <expbody>Distance_Algn2Terrain = TO_Slab-Terrain_elev to ft</expbody>
                <expresult> = 22.671 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Derived vertical distance from the notebook pier slab crown to the retained terrain elevation.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_026_Distance_Algn2Terrain" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">This derived distance supplies the full height available before subtracting the slab, beam-to-cap distance, and part of the cap depth in the exposed-pile expression. It is a height difference, not the terrain’s project elevation.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Thickness_slab_peak = 6 in">
                <expbody>Thickness_slab_peak = 6 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Slab thickness at the deck crown.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_027_Thickness_slab_peak" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Pier.dxf dimension *D5379: 6 in. The old beam-to-cap and terrain inputs in this subsection still require confirmation for the revised section.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Distance_topMidBeam_topCap = Beam_depth+BearingPlane_aboveCap to ft in">
                <expbody>Distance_topMidBeam_topCap = Beam_depth+BearingPlane_aboveCap to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 3 ft 8.562 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Derived beam-top-to-cap-top distance (legacy variable name).</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_028_Distance_topMidBeam_topCap" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Beam depth plus the selected pedestal, Type F pad and any separate bearing plate. The retained variable name supports existing references; this is now a derived dimension.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" id="paragraph0byy6f6o" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="PierCap_ht">
                <expbody>PierCap_ht</expbody>
                <expresult> = 3 ft 0 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Cap depth referenced from the single geometry input.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_029_Cap_ht" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">This display references the cap depth defined in General Bridge Layout; it is not another input.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="CapTop_aboveTerrain = CapTop_elev-Terrain_elev to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>CapTop_aboveTerrain = CapTop_elev-Terrain_elev to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 18 ft 2.915 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Cap-top height above the adopted terrain reference.</paragraph>
        <section name="CapDatumNote_CapTop_aboveTerrain" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Cap-top project elevation minus the adopted terrain elevation. The beam-soffit elevation is held fixed while changes to pedestal or pad thickness move the cap.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="CapCG_aboveTerrain = CapTop_aboveTerrain - PierCap_ht/2 to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>CapCG_aboveTerrain = CapTop_aboveTerrain - PierCap_ht/2 to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 16 ft 8.915 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Cap-centroid height above the adopted terrain reference.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="CapBottom_aboveTerrain = CapTop_aboveTerrain - PierCap_ht to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>CapBottom_aboveTerrain = CapTop_aboveTerrain - PierCap_ht to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 15 ft 2.915 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Cap-underside height above the adopted terrain reference.</paragraph>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Pile_ht_exposed = CapCG_aboveTerrain to ft">
                <expbody>Pile_ht_exposed = CapCG_aboveTerrain to ft</expbody>
                <expresult> = 16.743 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Legacy model-reference height to the cap centroid.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_030_Pile_ht_exposed" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">Retained variable name for existing references. This is terrain-to-cap-centroid height, not physical free pile length. CapBottom_aboveTerrain locates the cap underside; pile fixity and embedment require the actual foundation model.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="15' 4 5/16&quot; to ft">
                <expbody>15' 4 5/16" to ft</expbody>
                <expresult> = 15.359 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">CAD-reported exposed-pile height expressed in decimal feet.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_031_15_4_5_16_to_ft" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">Convert the entered feet-and-inches height to feet without changing the distance. This is the independent height identified as coming from CAD, so it can be compared with the preceding modeled-reference geometry result.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Pile_spacing = Pier_pile_spacingRatio*Pier_pile_diameter to in">
                <expbody>Pile_spacing = Pier_pile_spacingRatio*Pier_pile_diameter to in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 60 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1" fontweight="bold">Center-to-center distance between adjacent piles.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_BridgeGeometry_032_Pile_spacing" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="10" level="1">Measure from the center of one pile to the center of the next. This input is converted to inches for display and is divided by the pile-width input to express spacing as a number of pile widths. It is not the clear gap between pile surfaces.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph level="1" />
        <paragraph level="1" fontweight="bold" />
        <heading>Bearing, Backwall, and Pier Geometry — Supplied Schematic</heading>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Source: user-supplied FIB 36 bearing geometry schematic, added September 22, 2026. Non-skewed longitudinal elevations; deck omitted; not to scale. The following data reproduce the drawing and its dimension chains.</paragraph>
        <section name="TypeFBearingSchematics" capture="False" hide="false">
            <embed spacingafter="12">
                <canvas name="TypeFEndBent" title="Upright end-bent bearing and centered pile" unit="in" size="6.5 in; 5.65 in; scaletofit">
                    <include target="Library.Geometry" />
                    <planecontainer origin="0.1,5.4,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" textcolor="#29333D" fontweight="bold"><textvalue>END BENT — BEARING OFFSET / CENTERED PILE</textvalue></planecontainer>
                    <planecontainer origin="0.1,5.12,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Longitudinal elevation | Span is to the right | Not to scale</textvalue></planecontainer>
                    <plot formula="PlotLines([1.3,1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBentCap_width/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBentCap_width/(1 in),1.3,1.3],[1.55,1.55,2.85,2.85,1.55])" linecolor="#667887" linethickness="1" />
                    <plot formula="PlotLines([1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_rearFaceInset/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_rearFaceInset/(1 in)+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Backwall_thickness_shown/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_rearFaceInset/(1 in)+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Backwall_thickness_shown/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_rearFaceInset/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_rearFaceInset/(1 in)],[2.85,2.85,4.05,4.05,2.85])" linecolor="#667887" linethickness="1" />
                    <plot formula="PlotLines([1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_rearFaceInset/(1 in)+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Backwall_thickness_shown/(1 in)+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_beamEndClear/(1 in),6.1,6.1,1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_rearFaceInset/(1 in)+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Backwall_thickness_shown/(1 in)+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_beamEndClear/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_rearFaceInset/(1 in)+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Backwall_thickness_shown/(1 in)+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_beamEndClear/(1 in)],[3.21,3.21,4.05,4.05,3.21])" linecolor="#667887" linethickness="1" />
                    <plot formula="PlotLines([1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_bearingCL_fromRear/(1 in)-.035*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Bearing_pad_length/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_bearingCL_fromRear/(1 in)+.035*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Bearing_pad_length/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_bearingCL_fromRear/(1 in)+.035*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Bearing_pad_length/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_bearingCL_fromRear/(1 in)-.035*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Bearing_pad_length/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_bearingCL_fromRear/(1 in)-.035*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Bearing_pad_length/(1 in)],[3.08,3.08,3.21,3.21,3.08])" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="1" />
                    <plot formula="PlotLines([1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBentPedestal_fromRear/(1 in),1.3+.07*(BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBentPedestal_fromRear+BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Pedestal_length_endBent)/(1 in),1.3+.07*(BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBentPedestal_fromRear+BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Pedestal_length_endBent)/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBentPedestal_fromRear/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBentPedestal_fromRear/(1 in)],[2.85,2.85,3.08,3.08,2.85])" linecolor="#667887" linethickness="1" />
                    <plot formula="PlotLines([1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileCL_fromRear/(1 in)-.035*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileWidth/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileCL_fromRear/(1 in)+.035*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileWidth/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileCL_fromRear/(1 in)+.035*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileWidth/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileCL_fromRear/(1 in)-.035*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileWidth/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileCL_fromRear/(1 in)-.035*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileWidth/(1 in)],[0.7,0.7,1.55+1.3*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileEmbed/BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBentCap_depth,1.55+1.3*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileEmbed/BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBentCap_depth,0.7])" linecolor="#667887" linethickness="1" />
                    <plot formula="PlotLines([1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileCL_fromRear/(1 in),1.3+.07*BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBent_pileCL_fromRear/(1 in)],[0.65,2.78])" linecolor="#667887" linethickness="0.8" />
