                </canvas>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="8">Both bearing rows remain 10.5 in from the pier centerline, with a 21-in row spacing. Beam, pad, pedestal and cap are shown in their physical vertical order.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">The 12-in shown dimension is the backwall thickness. Bearing-centerline clearance follows the selected pad length and the separate beam-end/backwall clearance.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_length = 10 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Bearing_pad_length = 10 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Type F pad length along the beam (FDOT Index 400-510).</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_Bearing_pad_length" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Transcribed from the supplied schematic. Dimensions are measured along the beam for the non-skewed arrangement shown.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <section name="PedestalGeometry6in" capture="False" hide="false">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pedestal_ht = 6 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>Pedestal_ht = 6 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Selected pedestal height above cap top.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pedestal_width = 42 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>Pedestal_width = 42 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Adopted pedestal width transverse to the beam.</paragraph>
            <section name="TypeFNote_Pedestal_width" capture="False" hide="true">
                <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">The previous measured section has area 1.4544 ft² and perimeter 7.7601 ft. A 42-in width, 5-in height and two 3/4-in upper chamfers reproduce both measurements within their displayed precision. Retain that inferred width and chamfer geometry with the new 6-in height; verify against the final detail.</paragraph>
            </section>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pedestal_chamfer = 3/4 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>Pedestal_chamfer = 3/4 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Retained upper-corner chamfer dimension.</paragraph>
            <section name="TypeFNote_Pedestal_chamfer" capture="False" hide="true">
                <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Two triangular chamfer deductions are used in the transverse section. This geometry reproduces the previous measured area and perimeter; it is a quantity-model assumption pending final detailing.</paragraph>
            </section>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pedestal_area = Pedestal_width*Pedestal_ht-Pedestal_chamfer^2 to ft^2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Pedestal_area = Pedestal_width*Pedestal_ht-Pedestal_chamfer^2 to ft^2</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 1.746 ft^2</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Net pedestal transverse area after two top chamfers.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pedestal_length_pier = PierCap_width to ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Pedestal_length_pier = PierCap_width to ft</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 4 ft</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Pier pedestal length along the beam, spanning the cap width.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pedestal_count_pier = Beam_count" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Pedestal_count_pier = Beam_count</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 2</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Two continuous pier pedestals, each supporting one bearing from each span.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pedestal_volume_pier = Pedestal_count_pier*Pedestal_area*Pedestal_length_pier to ft^3" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Pedestal_volume_pier = Pedestal_count_pier*Pedestal_area*Pedestal_length_pier to ft^3</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 13.969 ft^3</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Total concrete in the two pier pedestals.</paragraph>
            <heading level="1" keepwithnext="True">End-bent pedestals — separate from pier</heading>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBentPedestal_ht = 6 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBentPedestal_ht = 6 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Established end-bent height; independent of the pier pedestal input.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBentPedestal_width = 42 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBentPedestal_width = 42 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Established transverse width, measured across the beam.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBentPedestal_chamfer = 3/4 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBentPedestal_chamfer = 3/4 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Established two top chamfers, retaining the quantity convention.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBentPedestal_area = EndBentPedestal_width*EndBentPedestal_ht-EndBentPedestal_chamfer^2 to ft^2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBentPedestal_area = EndBentPedestal_width*EndBentPedestal_ht-EndBentPedestal_chamfer^2 to ft^2</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 1.746 ft^2</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">End-bent transverse area; pier quantities retain Pedestal_area.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBentPedestal_fromRear = EndBent_rearFaceInset+Backwall_thickness_shown to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBentPedestal_fromRear = EndBent_rearFaceInset+Backwall_thickness_shown to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 12 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Pedestal starts at the backwall front; 12 in from the cap rear face.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pedestal_length_endBent = EndBentCap_width-EndBentPedestal_fromRear to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>Pedestal_length_endBent = EndBentCap_width-EndBentPedestal_fromRear to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 30 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">User response: 42-in cap less 12-in backwall gives 30 in along the beam. The pier pedestal remains 48 in.</paragraph>
            <section name="TypeFNote_Pedestal_length_endBent" capture="False" hide="true">
                <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Retains the existing quantity-sheet length. The 6-in height and inferred transverse width are adopted at both end bents; verify the end-bent footprint and cap edge clearances.</paragraph>
            </section>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pedestal_count_endBent = 2*Beam_count" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Pedestal_count_endBent = 2*Beam_count</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 4</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Four end-bent pedestals across the two end bents.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pedestal_volume_endBent = Pedestal_count_endBent*EndBentPedestal_area*Pedestal_length_endBent to ft^3" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Pedestal_volume_endBent = Pedestal_count_endBent*EndBentPedestal_area*Pedestal_length_endBent to ft^3</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 17.461 ft^3</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Total pedestal concrete at both end bents.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_separatePlateThickness = 0 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>Bearing_separatePlateThickness = 0 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Separate plate thickness included in the support stack.</paragraph>
            <section name="TypeFNote_Bearing_separatePlateThickness" capture="False" hide="true">
                <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">No separate plate thickness is established in this geometry. Zero represents the adopted pedestal-plus-pad stack; enter the thickness of any required separate plate before issuing seat elevations. The embedded beam plate is included in the defined beam soffit.</paragraph>
            </section>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_soffit_elev = BO_LowBeam to ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_soffit_elev = BO_LowBeam to ft</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 44.483 ft</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Adopted low-beam soffit elevation for the cap datum.</paragraph>
            <section name="TypeFNote_Bearing_soffit_elev" capture="False" hide="true">
                <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">The notebook pier soffit now supplies this reference. The common bearing-plane wind model uses this reference. Resolve crossfall, beam-end grades and individual seat elevations in final detailing; this is not a claim that all four physical soffits have identical elevations.</paragraph>
            </section>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="CapTop_elev = Bearing_soffit_elev-BearingPlane_aboveCap to ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>CapTop_elev = Bearing_soffit_elev-BearingPlane_aboveCap to ft</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 43.769 ft</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Cap-top elevation from the fixed beam soffit and support stack.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="CapCG_elev = CapTop_elev-PierCap_ht/2 to ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>CapCG_elev = CapTop_elev-PierCap_ht/2 to ft</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 42.269 ft</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Cap-centroid elevation from the single 36-in cap depth.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="CapBottom_elev = CapTop_elev-PierCap_ht to ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>CapBottom_elev = CapTop_elev-PierCap_ht to ft</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 40.769 ft</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Cap-underside elevation from the single cap-depth input.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Terrain_elev = 25.5264 ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Terrain_elev = 25.5264 ft</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Retained terrain project elevation: former 47.672-ft slab datum minus 22.1456-ft terrain distance. It stays at 25.5264 ft when the notebook slab datum changes.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <section name="TypeFPadGeometry" capture="False" hide="false">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_type = &quot;F&quot;" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_type = "F"</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Selected pad type for the two-beam bridge.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_width = 32 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_width = 32 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Type F pad width transverse to the beam.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_thickness = 2.5625 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_thickness = 2.5625 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Type F overall pad thickness.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_G = 110 psi" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_G = 110 psi</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Type F elastomer shear modulus.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_internalLayers = 3" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_internalLayers = 3</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Number of internal elastomer layers.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_internalThickness = 1/2 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_internalThickness = 1/2 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Thickness of each internal elastomer layer.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_cover = 1/4 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_cover = 1/4 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Top and bottom elastomer cover thickness.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_steelLayers = 4" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_steelLayers = 4</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Number of 10-gage steel laminates.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_shearLimit = 1 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_shearLimit = 1 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Type F limiting shear deflection (SPI 400-510).</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_skew = 0 deg" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_skew = 0 deg</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Adopted bearing skew for the non-skewed project layout.</paragraph>
            <section name="TypeFNote_Bearing_pad_skew" capture="False" hide="true">
                <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Bearing skew is relative to the direction of beam rotation; it is not the wind incidence angle. Verify against final bearing details. The Type F table has separate 0–5 degree and 0–30 degree limits.</paragraph>
            </section>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_area = Bearing_pad_length*Bearing_pad_width to in^2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_area = Bearing_pad_length*Bearing_pad_width to in^2</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 320 in^2</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Gross pad plan area.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_volume = Bearing_pad_area*Bearing_pad_thickness to ft^3" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_volume = Bearing_pad_area*Bearing_pad_thickness to ft^3</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 0.475 ft^3</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Gross composite volume of one Type F pad.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_count = 2*Beam_count*2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_count = 2*Beam_count*2</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 8</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Project pad count: two spans, two beams and two ends per beam.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_pad_totalVolume = Bearing_pad_count*Bearing_pad_volume to ft^3" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_pad_totalVolume = Bearing_pad_count*Bearing_pad_volume to ft^3</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 3.796 ft^3</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Gross composite volume for the eight project pads.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="BearingPadBase_CapCG = BearingPlane_CapCG - Bearing_pad_thickness to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>BearingPadBase_CapCG = BearingPlane_CapCG - Bearing_pad_thickness to ft in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 2 ft 0 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Pad base above the cap centroid.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Bearing_supportBuildup = Pedestal_ht+Bearing_separatePlateThickness to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Bearing_supportBuildup = Pedestal_ht+Bearing_separatePlateThickness to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 6 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Non-pad support buildup: pedestal plus any separate plate.</paragraph>
            <section name="TypeFNote_Bearing_supportBuildup" capture="False" hide="true">
                <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">The 6-in pedestal and any separate plate are explicit inputs. The cap-top elevation is derived below the fixed beam soffit; it is not held fixed independently.</paragraph>
            </section>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Check_TypeF_support = If(Bearing_supportBuildup &gt;= 0 in, &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Check_TypeF_support = If(Bearing_supportBuildup &gt;= 0 in, "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody>
                    <expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Check that the pad fits within the adopted cap-to-beam buildup.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Pier_padEdge_clear = PierCap_width/2-PierCL_bearingCL-Bearing_pad_length/2 to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Pier_padEdge_clear = PierCap_width/2-PierCL_bearingCL-Bearing_pad_length/2 to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 8.5 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Outer edge of pier pad to cap face for the non-skewed layout.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="Check_TypeF_capEdge = If(And(Bearing_pad_skew == 0 deg, Pier_padEdge_clear &gt;= 4 in), &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>Check_TypeF_capEdge = If(And(Bearing_pad_skew == 0 deg, Pier_padEdge_clear &gt;= 4 in), "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody>
                    <expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Check the illustrated 4-in minimum cap-edge clearance at zero skew.</paragraph>
            <section name="TypeFNote_Check_TypeF_capEdge" capture="False" hide="true">
                <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">For nonzero bearing skew, recalculate the projected footprint and edge clearances from the skewed detail; this zero-skew check intentionally fails outside its stated scope.</paragraph>
            </section>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">
                <link address="https://fdotwww.blob.core.windows.net/sitefinity/docs/default-source/design/standardplans/2027/idx/400-510.pdf">Pad dimensions and construction: FDOT Index 400-510, FY 2026–27</link>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">
                <link address="https://fdotwww.blob.core.windows.net/sitefinity/docs/default-source/design/standardplans/2027/spi/spi-400-510.pdf">Pad limiting parameters: FDOT SPI 400-510, FY 2026–27</link>
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="BeamEnd_padEdge = 4 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>BeamEnd_padEdge = 4 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Beam end to nearest bearing pad edge.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_BeamEnd_padEdge" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Transcribed from the supplied schematic. Dimensions are measured along the beam for the non-skewed arrangement shown.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="BeamEnd_bearingCL = BeamEnd_padEdge + Bearing_pad_length/2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>BeamEnd_bearingCL = BeamEnd_padEdge + Bearing_pad_length/2</expbody>
                <expresult> = 9 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">J: beam end to bearing centerline.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_BeamEnd_bearingCL" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Beam end to bearing centerline equals the beam-end-to-pad-edge offset plus half the selected pad length.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="BeamEnd_backwallClear_min = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>BeamEnd_backwallClear_min = 3 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Minimum beam-end clearance to front face of backwall.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_BeamEnd_backwallClear_min" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Source schematic labels c ≥ 3 in. and cites SDM 12.6.I. This is a minimum shown in the supplied reference, not a thermal-movement clearance calculation.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="BearingCL_backwall_min = BeamEnd_bearingCL + BeamEnd_backwallClear_min" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>BearingCL_backwall_min = BeamEnd_bearingCL + BeamEnd_backwallClear_min</expbody>
                <expresult> = 12 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Minimum bearing centerline to front face of backwall.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_BearingCL_backwall_min" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Transcribed from the supplied schematic. Dimensions are measured along the beam for the non-skewed arrangement shown.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="PadEdge_backwall_min = BearingCL_backwall_min - Bearing_pad_length/2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>PadEdge_backwall_min = BearingCL_backwall_min - Bearing_pad_length/2</expbody>
                <expresult> = 7 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Minimum nearest pad edge to front face of backwall.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_PadEdge_backwall_min" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Transcribed from the supplied schematic. Dimensions are measured along the beam for the non-skewed arrangement shown.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Backwall_thickness_shown = 12 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Backwall_thickness_shown = 12 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Illustrated backwall thickness.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_Backwall_thickness_shown" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Source schematic states generally ≥ 12 in., cites SDM 12.6.B., and directs increasing thickness as required by design.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Backwall_thickness_min_ref = 12 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Backwall_thickness_min_ref = 12 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">General minimum backwall thickness stated by the schematic.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_Backwall_thickness_min_ref" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Reference value transcribed from the supplied schematic; the illustrated 12 in. thickness is not a completed backwall design.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Pier_beamEndGap = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Pier_beamEndGap = 3 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Nominal gap between squared beam ends at the interior pier.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_Pier_beamEndGap" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Transcribed from the supplied schematic. Dimensions are measured along the beam for the non-skewed arrangement shown.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="PierCL_beamEnd = Pier_beamEndGap/2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>PierCL_beamEnd = Pier_beamEndGap/2</expbody>
                <expresult> = 1.5 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Pier centerline to each adjacent beam end.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_PierCL_beamEnd" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Transcribed from the supplied schematic. Dimensions are measured along the beam for the non-skewed arrangement shown.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="PierCL_bearingCL = BeamEnd_bearingCL + PierCL_beamEnd" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>PierCL_bearingCL = BeamEnd_bearingCL + PierCL_beamEnd</expbody>
                <expresult> = 10.5 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">K: pier centerline to each bearing centerline.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_PierCL_bearingCL" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Transcribed from the supplied schematic. Dimensions are measured along the beam for the non-skewed arrangement shown.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Pier_bearingCL_spacing = 2*PierCL_bearingCL" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Pier_bearingCL_spacing = 2*PierCL_bearingCL</expbody>
                <expresult> = 21 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Longitudinal spacing between bearing centerlines across the pier.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_Pier_bearingCL_spacing" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">The longitudinal bearing-row spacing equals twice the live pier-centerline-to-bearing-centerline offset.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Source citations reproduced from drawing: 2026 SDM 12.6.I and 12.6.B. Source provisions have not been independently reverified in this geometry transcription.</paragraph>
        <heading>Thickened Deck Ends — Supplied Concept and Geometry</heading>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Source: user-supplied “Pedestrian Bridge – Thickened Deck End Concept,” added September 22, 2026. Concept only; not to scale. Drawing cites SDG 4.2.4.D and SDM Figure 15.5-1; retain its instruction to verify project edition and final detailing.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" horzalign="Center">
            <image source="G2ThickenedDeckEndSchematic" width="660" height="495.0" />
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">The deck width, inside-parapet width, beam spacing, and FIB 36 depth agree with the existing two-beam geometry. The equations below reference those existing variables.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="DeckEnd_width = Deck_out2out" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckEnd_width = Deck_out2out</expbody>
                <expresult> = 13 ft 7 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Deck out-to-out width.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_DeckEnd_width" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Live reference to the existing geometry input; agrees with the dimension shown in the supplied thickened-end schematic.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="DeckEnd_insideParapets = Dist_insideParapets" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckEnd_insideParapets = Dist_insideParapets</expbody>
                <expresult> = 12 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Clear width between inside parapet faces.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_DeckEnd_insideParapets" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Live reference to the existing geometry input; agrees with the dimension shown in the supplied thickened-end schematic.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="DeckEnd_beamSpacing = Beam_spacing" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckEnd_beamSpacing = Beam_spacing</expbody>
                <expresult> = 8 ft 7 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Beam center-to-center spacing.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_DeckEnd_beamSpacing" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Live reference to the existing geometry input; agrees with the dimension shown in the supplied thickened-end schematic.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="DeckEnd_beamDepth = Beam_depth" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckEnd_beamDepth = Beam_depth</expbody>
                <expresult> = 3 ft</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Nominal FIB 36 depth.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_DeckEnd_beamDepth" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Live reference to the existing geometry input; agrees with the dimension shown in the supplied thickened-end schematic.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="DeckEnd_length_min = 2 ft 6 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckEnd_length_min = 2 ft 6 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Minimum thickened-end length into the span.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_DeckEnd_length_min" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Measured from the deck end into the span in the zero-skew concept. The supplied drawing calls for additional reinforcing at similar spacing when this length exceeds 2 ft 6 in.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="DeckEnd_addedDepth_min = 4 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckEnd_addedDepth_min = 4 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Minimum additional depth below the normal deck soffit.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_DeckEnd_addedDepth_min" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">The supplied drawing also calls for the thickened soffit to match the bottom of the FIB top flange. Actual total thickened depth requires the local slab, haunch, and flange geometry; 4 in. is a minimum addition, not an independently established final thickness.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="DeckEnd_detailBeamSpacing_max = 14 ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckEnd_detailBeamSpacing_max = 14 ft</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Maximum beam spacing stated for the reference detail.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_DeckEnd_detailBeamSpacing_max" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Transcribed from the supplied schematic. Dimensions are measured along the beam for the non-skewed arrangement shown.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="DeckEnd_detailSkew_max = 35 deg" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckEnd_detailSkew_max = 35 deg</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Maximum skew stated for the reference detail.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_DeckEnd_detailSkew_max" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Transcribed from the supplied schematic. Dimensions are measured along the beam for the non-skewed arrangement shown.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="DeckEnd_topBarSkew_limit = 15 deg" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckEnd_topBarSkew_limit = 15 deg</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Skew threshold separating the two top-reinforcement notes.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_DeckEnd_topBarSkew_limit" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Transcribed from the supplied schematic. Dimensions are measured along the beam for the non-skewed arrangement shown.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="DeckEnd_topSteelArea_min = 2.48 in^2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckEnd_topSteelArea_min = 2.48 in^2</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Minimum top reinforcement area stated for skew ≤ 15°.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_DeckEnd_topSteelArea_min" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Source drawing: supplemental #5 plus normal top steel, As ≥ 2.48 in² within the thickened end; top end reinforcement is below the normal top deck mat.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="DeckEnd_topBarCount_highSkew = 8" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckEnd_topBarCount_highSkew = 8</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Number of #5 top bars stated for skew &gt; 15°.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_DeckEnd_topBarCount_highSkew" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Source drawing: 8–#5 top bars parallel to skew, within the stated detail applicability limits.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="DeckEnd_bottomBarCount = 7" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckEnd_bottomBarCount = 7</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Number of #5 bottom bars shown.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_DeckEnd_bottomBarCount" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Source drawing: 7–#5 bottom bars parallel to skew.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="DeckEnd_distributionSpacing = 12 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckEnd_distributionSpacing = 12 in</expbody>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Spacing of #4 distribution bars shown.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_G2Schematic_DeckEnd_distributionSpacing" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Transcribed from the supplied schematic. Dimensions are measured along the beam for the non-skewed arrangement shown.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Application and reinforcement notes from the supplied concept:</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">• Apply at deck discontinuities without full-depth diaphragms.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">• Continuous deck over the interior pier: no thickening per the supplied concept.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">• Top deck surface remains flat; thickening is below the normal soffit between beams.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">• Thickened soffit matches the bottom of the FIB top flange, with at least 4 in. additional depth as labeled.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">• Skew ≤ 15°: supplemental #5 bars plus normal top steel provide at least 2.48 in² within the thickened end.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">• Skew &gt; 15°: 8–#5 top bars parallel to skew; 7–#5 bottom bars parallel to skew; #4 distribution bars at 12 in.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">• Top end reinforcement is below the normal top deck mat. For a thickened-end length greater than 2 ft 6 in., add bars at similar spacing.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="12">• Reference-detail limits: beam spacing ≤ 14 ft and skew ≤ 35°. The drawings do not establish the project skew or a final reinforcing design.</paragraph>
        <heading id="headingBridgeGeometry_2Beam8" style="Uplift Heading 1">
            <paragraphlabel numbergroup="heading">6.</paragraphlabel>
             Bearing reference for wind-load transfer
        </heading>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="CapTop_CapCG = PierCap_ht/2 to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>CapTop_CapCG = PierCap_ht/2 to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 1 ft 6 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Cap top above the cap centroid.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="CapBottom_CapCG = -PierCap_ht/2 to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>CapBottom_CapCG = -PierCap_ht/2 to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = -1 ft 6 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Cap underside relative to the cap centroid.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="BearingPlane_CapCG = CapTop_CapCG + BearingPlane_aboveCap to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showformula="True" showidentifier="True" showresult="True" seplines="False" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: [ft]})">
                <expbody>BearingPlane_CapCG = CapTop_CapCG + BearingPlane_aboveCap to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 2 ft 2.562 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Bearing plane above the cap centroid.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_006_BridgeGeometry_2Beam" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">Add half the single cap depth to the adopted support buildup. The concrete wind envelope begins at this beam-soffit plane; its centroid and fence levels are derived upward from it.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="BearingPlane_aboveCap = Pedestal_ht+Bearing_pad_thickness+Bearing_separatePlateThickness to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showformula="True" showidentifier="True" showresult="True" seplines="False" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: [in]})">
                <expbody>BearingPlane_aboveCap = Pedestal_ht+Bearing_pad_thickness+Bearing_separatePlateThickness to in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 8.563 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold">Beam-soffit / bearing-plane height above cap top: pedestal, pad and any separate plate.</paragraph>
        <section name="EqNotes_007_BridgeGeometry_2Beam" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">Support stack is explicitly defined by the selected pedestal and bearing pad. Cap elevations and wind arms follow this stack; no independent beam-to-cap height is entered.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="12" spacingbefore="6">
            <dynexp formula="Check_bearingDatum = If(And(PierCap_ht &gt; 0 ft, BearingPlane_aboveCap &gt;= 0 in, Abs(BearingPlane_CapCG-CapTop_CapCG-BearingPlane_aboveCap)&lt;0.000001 in), &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showformula="False" showidentifier="False" showresult="True" seplines="False">
                <expresult>✓ PASS</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7">Check cap depth, support clearance and datum consistency.</paragraph>
        <section name="CapDatumNote_Check_bearingDatum" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">PASS checks the adopted pedestal, pad and cap geometry chain only. It does not verify the wind envelope, individual seat grades or separate bearing-plate requirements.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <heading level="1">9. Individual pier-bearing tributaries</heading>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">B1/B2 receive Span 1; B3/B4 receive Span 2. B1/B3 are on the negative-transverse beam line. The entered project span lengths remain the load-model spans. Their alignment datums are not established as bearing-to-bearing dimensions; no undocumented end offset is subtracted.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="PierTrib_1 = Span_1/2 to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>PierTrib_1 = Span_1/2 to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 53 ft 8.100 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Span 1 tributary length to its pier bearing row.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="PierTrib_2 = Span_2/2 to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>PierTrib_2 = Span_2/2 to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 52 ft 5.400 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Span 2 tributary length to its pier bearing row.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="Deck_overhang = (Deck_out2out-Beam_spacing)/2 to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>Deck_overhang = (Deck_out2out-Beam_spacing)/2 to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 2 ft 6 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Deck edge to beam centerline for the symmetric two-beam section.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="DeckTrib_minus = Beam_spacing/2+Deck_overhang to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckTrib_minus = Beam_spacing/2+Deck_overhang to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 6 ft 9.5 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Deck tributary width assigned to the negative-transverse beam.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="DeckTrib_plus = Deck_out2out-DeckTrib_minus to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>DeckTrib_plus = Deck_out2out-DeckTrib_minus to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 6 ft 9.5 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Deck tributary width assigned to the positive-transverse beam.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="WalkTrib_minus = Bridge_clearWidth/2 to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>WalkTrib_minus = Bridge_clearWidth/2 to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 6 ft 0 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Pedestrian loaded width assigned to the negative-transverse beam.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="WalkTrib_plus = Bridge_clearWidth-WalkTrib_minus to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                <expbody>WalkTrib_plus = Bridge_clearWidth-WalkTrib_minus to ft in</expbody>
                <expresult> = 6 ft 0 in</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Pedestrian loaded width assigned to the positive-transverse beam.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Equal transverse gravity sharing follows the centered, symmetric section. Unequal longitudinal bearing loads are retained from the separate span tributaries. Haunch allocation retains the entered total volume and equivalent uniform longitudinal distribution.</paragraph>
        <section name="EndBentGeometry" capture="False" hide="false">
            <heading level="0" keepwithnext="True">End-bent geometry for FBMP entry</heading>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">Current geometry for both end bents: cap and pile dimensions follow the 8 October 2026 End Bent 1 cap report; applicability to both end bents is confirmed by the user. Bearing spacing and the backwall/beam-end placement chain remain the journal basis. End Bent 1 analysis results are recorded separately from this shared geometry.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" leftindent="0" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBentCap_width = 42 in to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBentCap_width = 42 in to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 42 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0">Cap width along the bridge.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" leftindent="0" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBentCap_depth = 36 in to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBentCap_depth = 36 in to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 36 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0">Cap depth.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" leftindent="0" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_bearingSpacing = Beam_spacing to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_bearingSpacing = Beam_spacing to ft in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 8 ft 7 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0">Same transverse bearing spacing as the two-beam bridge.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="2" leftindent="0" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_BearingPlane_CapCG = EndBentCap_depth/2+EndBentPedestal_ht+Bearing_pad_thickness+Bearing_separatePlateThickness to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_BearingPlane_CapCG = EndBentCap_depth/2+EndBentPedestal_ht+Bearing_pad_thickness+Bearing_separatePlateThickness to ft in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 2 ft 2.562 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0">Bearing plane above the end-bent cap centroid, using the separate 6-in end-bent pedestal and Type F pad.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="2">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_rearFaceInset = 0 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_rearFaceInset = 0 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">Adopted layout: back face of backwall flush with rear cap edge. Positive inset moves the backwall toward the span. This placement is explicit because the source schematic does not dimension a rear-face inset.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="2">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_beamEndClear = BeamEnd_backwallClear_min to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_beamEndClear = BeamEnd_backwallClear_min to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 3 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">Adopted beam-end clearance from the geometry schematic; initially its 3-in minimum. This is a layout input, not a completed movement-clearance check.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="2">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_pileCL_fromRear = EndBentCap_width/2 to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_pileCL_fromRear = EndBentCap_width/2 to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 21 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">Pile line centered within the cap width along the bridge, per user clarification.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="2">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_bearingCL_fromRear = EndBent_rearFaceInset+Backwall_thickness_shown+EndBent_beamEndClear+BeamEnd_bearingCL to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_bearingCL_fromRear = EndBent_rearFaceInset+Backwall_thickness_shown+EndBent_beamEndClear+BeamEnd_bearingCL to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 24 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">Rear cap edge to bearing line: rear-face inset + backwall thickness + beam-end clearance + beam-end-to-bearing distance.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="2">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_bearingOffset = EndBent_bearingCL_fromRear-EndBent_pileCL_fromRear to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_bearingOffset = EndBent_bearingCL_fromRear-EndBent_pileCL_fromRear to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 3 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">Bearing eccentricity toward the adjacent span relative to the centered pile/cap line. It follows the live rear-face, backwall, beam-end and half-cap-width chain. Verify this reference point against the exact analysis model.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="2">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_padFrontClear = EndBentCap_width-EndBent_bearingCL_fromRear-Bearing_pad_length/2 to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_padFrontClear = EndBentCap_width-EndBent_bearingCL_fromRear-Bearing_pad_length/2 to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 13 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">Pad edge to span-side cap edge in the zero-skew layout. This geometric clearance is not a bearing-seat design check.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="2">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_checkLayout = If(And(EndBent_rearFaceInset &gt;= 0 in,EndBent_beamEndClear &gt;= BeamEnd_backwallClear_min,EndBent_padFrontClear &gt;= 0 in),&quot;PASS - PAD WITHIN CAP / MINIMUM GAP&quot;,&quot;REVIEW GEOMETRY&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_checkLayout = If(And(EndBent_rearFaceInset &gt;= 0 in,EndBent_beamEndClear &gt;= BeamEnd_backwallClear_min,EndBent_padFrontClear &gt;= 0 in),"PASS - PAD WITHIN CAP / MINIMUM GAP","REVIEW GEOMETRY")</expbody>
                    <expresult> = PASS - PAD WITHIN CAP / MINIMUM GAP</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">Checks the pad dimension chain only. The end-bent pedestal occupies the remaining 30 in between the backwall front and cap front; the pier pedestal remains 48 in.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <section name="EndBentCurrentGeometry" capture="False" hide="false">
            <heading level="0" keepwithnext="True" pagebreakbefore="break">End-bent cap and pile layout — both end bents</heading>
            <embed spacingbefore="8" spacingafter="12" leftindent="0">
                <table name="EBCurrentGeometryContext" capture="False" colwidths="1:100, 2:420">
                    <stylerule range="A1:B4" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.7, &quot;#7189A6&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#7189A6&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenColumns&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);" vertalign="Center" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:B1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold" />
                    <stylerule range="A2:B4" background="#F1F5FA" />
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Basis</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Scope</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Source</textvalue></c>
                        <textcell capture="False">
                            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="3">Geometry notebook, model e9b41b8eaf, 19 October 2026 (decision D-036); mirrored in project_current/geometry/tables/B4_Geometry_CAD_Tables.xlsx. Replaces the End bent 1 Cap Design Report_10-8.html geometry (4-in end detail, 212-in cap).</paragraph>
                        </textcell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Application</textvalue></c>
                        <textcell capture="False">
                            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="3">Both end bents follow the controlling End Bent 1 geometry and reinforcement by user direction. Source forces are from End Bent 1.</paragraph>
                        </textcell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Status</textvalue></c>
                        <textcell capture="False">
                            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="3">Data record with unresolved detailing and model checks; not construction approval.</paragraph>
                        </textcell>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_pileCount = 4" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_pileCount = 4</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Square piles per cap.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_pileWidth = 18 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_pileWidth = 18 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Square pile width in both plan directions; not the pier pipe diameter.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_pileSpacing = 54 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_pileSpacing = 54 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Center-to-center spacing along the cap.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_edgeClear = 9 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_edgeClear = 9 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Entered actual pile-face edge-clearance allowance.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_pileTolerance = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_pileTolerance = 3 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Horizontal placement tolerance allowance, separate from bar clearance.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_pileEndClear = 27.5 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_pileEndClear = 27.5 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Clear distance from the outer pile face to the cap end; notebook CONFIG end_bents.*.pile_end_clear_in (D-026 235-in cap)</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_endDetail = EndBent_pileEndClear-EndBent_edgeClear-EndBent_pileTolerance to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_endDetail = EndBent_pileEndClear-EndBent_edgeClear-EndBent_pileTolerance to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 15.5 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Additional end allowance derived from the notebook pile end clearance; the previous 4-in input gave a 16-in pile end clearance and a 212-in cap.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_pileEmbed = 12 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_pileEmbed = 12 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Physical pile penetration above cap underside; separate from analysis node elevation.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_pileBarClear = 1 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_pileBarClear = 1 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Entered pile-surface to bar-surface gap; project/code applicability remains a review item.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_coverTop = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_coverTop = 3 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Clear cover to outside of transverse reinforcement.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_coverBottom = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_coverBottom = 3 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Clear cover to outside of transverse reinforcement.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_coverSide = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_coverSide = 3 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Clear cover to outside of transverse reinforcement.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PierCap_coverTop = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>PierCap_coverTop = 3 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Clear cover to the hoop, pier cap, top; moved here from C005 (removed 19 October 2026).</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PierCap_coverBottom = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>PierCap_coverBottom = 3 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Clear cover to the hoop, pier cap, bottom; moved here from C005 (removed 19 October 2026).</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PierCap_coverSide = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>PierCap_coverSide = 3 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Clear cover to the hoop, pier cap, sides; moved here from C005 (removed 19 October 2026).</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_count = 2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_count = 2</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Both end bents use this geometry by user confirmation.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_endFace = EndBent_edgeClear+EndBent_pileTolerance+EndBent_endDetail to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_endFace = EndBent_edgeClear+EndBent_pileTolerance+EndBent_endDetail to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 27.5 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Nominal end-to-outer-pile-face distance.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_endCenter = EndBent_endFace+EndBent_pileWidth/2 to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_endCenter = EndBent_endFace+EndBent_pileWidth/2 to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 36.5 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Left end to first pile center; equal right end distance.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBentCap_length = (EndBent_pileCount-1)*EndBent_pileSpacing+2*EndBent_endCenter to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBentCap_length = (EndBent_pileCount-1)*EndBent_pileSpacing+2*EndBent_endCenter to ft in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 19 ft 7 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Overall cap length along the pile row.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_cheekThickness = 8 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_cheekThickness = 8 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Cheek web thickness outside each cap end; notebook CONFIG end_bents.*.cheek_thickness_in (D-026)</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_lugProjection = 6 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_lugProjection = 6 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Bottom and rear lug projection; notebook CONFIG end_bents.*.lug_projection_in (D-026 DXF)</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_lugWidth = 5.5 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_lugWidth = 5.5 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Lug width on the cheek outer face; notebook CONFIG end_bents.*.lug_width_in (D-026 DXF)</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_mseJoint = 0.5 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False" style="Required Input">
                    <expbody>EndBent_mseJoint = 0.5 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">MSE panel joint to cheek and lug faces; notebook CONFIG end_bents.*.mse_joint_in (D-026)</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBentCage_envelope = EndBentCap_length+2*EndBent_cheekThickness to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBentCage_envelope = EndBentCap_length+2*EndBent_cheekThickness to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 251 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Out-to-out of the cap with both cheek webs; the cap cages and the cap design reports use this 251-in envelope (D-027)</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_pileClearSpacing = EndBent_pileSpacing-EndBent_pileWidth to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_pileClearSpacing = EndBent_pileSpacing-EndBent_pileWidth to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 36 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Clear spacing between nominal square pile faces.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBentCap_area = EndBentCap_width*EndBentCap_depth to ft^2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBentCap_area = EndBentCap_width*EndBentCap_depth to ft^2</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 10.5 ft^2</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Gross rectangular cap section; excludes backwall and pedestal.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBentCap_volume = EndBentCap_area*EndBentCap_length to ft^3" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBentCap_volume = EndBentCap_area*EndBentCap_length to ft^3</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 205.625 ft^3</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Gross concrete per cap, before pile deductions.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBentCaps_volume = EndBent_count*EndBentCap_volume to ft^3" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBentCaps_volume = EndBent_count*EndBentCap_volume to ft^3</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 411.25 ft^3</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Gross rectangular caps at both end bents.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBentCap_DC = EndBentCap_volume*PedBridgeWeights_2Beams.I29 to kip" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBentCap_DC = EndBentCap_volume*PedBridgeWeights_2Beams.I29 to kip</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 30.844 kip</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Cap-only self-weight using the existing project concrete unit weight. Do not add twice if the foundation model generates cap self-weight.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_P1_station = EndBent_endCenter+0*EndBent_pileSpacing to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_P1_station = EndBent_endCenter+0*EndBent_pileSpacing to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 36.5 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Pile P1 center station from the left cap end.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_P2_station = EndBent_endCenter+1*EndBent_pileSpacing to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_P2_station = EndBent_endCenter+1*EndBent_pileSpacing to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 90.5 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Pile P2 center station from the left cap end.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_P3_station = EndBent_endCenter+2*EndBent_pileSpacing to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_P3_station = EndBent_endCenter+2*EndBent_pileSpacing to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 144.5 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Pile P3 center station from the left cap end.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="EndBent_P4_station = EndBent_endCenter+3*EndBent_pileSpacing to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>EndBent_P4_station = EndBent_endCenter+3*EndBent_pileSpacing to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 198.5 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Pile P4 center station from the left cap end.</paragraph>
            <embed spacingbefore="8" spacingafter="12" leftindent="0">
                <table name="EBCurrentPileStations" capture="False" colwidths="1:70, 2:150, 3:150, 4:150">
                    <stylerule range="A1:D5" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.7, &quot;#6A9075&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#6A9075&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenColumns&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#6A9075&quot;);" vertalign="Center" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:D1" background="#DCECE0" fontweight="bold" />
                    <stylerule range="A2:D5" background="#EFF7F1" />
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Pile</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Center (in)</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Left face (in)</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Right face (in)</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>P1</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EndBent_P1_station to in"><num>36.5 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EndBent_P1_station-EndBent_pileWidth/2 to in"><num>27.5 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EndBent_P1_station+EndBent_pileWidth/2 to in"><num>45.5 in</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>P2</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EndBent_P2_station to in"><num>90.5 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EndBent_P2_station-EndBent_pileWidth/2 to in"><num>81.5 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EndBent_P2_station+EndBent_pileWidth/2 to in"><num>99.5 in</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>P3</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EndBent_P3_station to in"><num>144.5 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EndBent_P3_station-EndBent_pileWidth/2 to in"><num>135.5 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EndBent_P3_station+EndBent_pileWidth/2 to in"><num>153.5 in</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>P4</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EndBent_P4_station to in"><num>198.5 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EndBent_P4_station-EndBent_pileWidth/2 to in"><num>189.5 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EndBent_P4_station+EndBent_pileWidth/2 to in"><num>207.5 in</num></c>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Geometry/cage stations start at the left cap end. The source XML audit starts at the first pile center; add EndBent_endCenter to convert audit stations. Bearing audit stations 29.50 and 132.49 in therefore correspond to 66.00 and 168.99 in from the cap end (36.5-in first pile center). Their separation is 102.99 in, consistent with the journal’s 103-in bearing spacing to the XML’s displayed precision.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">
                <link address="#FBMPEndBent.EBCurrentDesignRecord">Current reinforcement, source forces and coherence register</link>
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <section name="PierCurrentGeometry" capture="False" hide="false">
            <heading level="0" keepwithnext="True">Current pier cap geometry — 9 October 2026</heading>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Pier Cap Design 10-9.html confirms the existing 48-in by 36-in cap and four 20-in pipe piles at 60-in centers. The live project geometry above remains the owner. The new record below completes the cap-end datum, physical embedment and gross quantity definitions. Pier pedestals remain 48 in long by the user’s prior direction.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PierCap_edgeClear = 9 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>PierCap_edgeClear = 9 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Entered pile-face edge-clearance allowance.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PierCap_pileTolerance = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>PierCap_pileTolerance = 3 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Horizontal pile placement tolerance.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PierCap_endDetail = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>PierCap_endDetail = 3 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Report additional end allowance (3 in; 15-in pile end clearance, as the notebook pier.pile_end_clear_in); C005 was removed from the journal on 19 October 2026 (T014).</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PierCap_pileEmbed = 12 in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>PierCap_pileEmbed = 12 in</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Physical embedment above cap underside; not an analysis elevation.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PierCap_endCenter = PierCap_endClear+Pier_pile_diameter/2 to in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>PierCap_endCenter = PierCap_endClear+Pier_pile_diameter/2 to in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 25 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">25-in cap-end to first pile-center datum shift.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PierCap_endCheck = If(Abs(PierCap_endClear-PierCap_edgeClear-PierCap_pileTolerance-PierCap_endDetail) &lt; 0.000001 in,&quot;MATCH&quot;,&quot;RECONCILE END ALLOWANCES&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>PierCap_endCheck = If(Abs(PierCap_endClear-PierCap_edgeClear-PierCap_pileTolerance-PierCap_endDetail) &lt; 0.000001 in,"MATCH","RECONCILE END ALLOWANCES")</expbody>
                    <expresult> = MATCH</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Checks 15 = 9 + 3 + 3 in against the existing shared end-face distance.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PierCap_area = PierCap_width*PierCap_ht to ft^2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>PierCap_area = PierCap_width*PierCap_ht to ft^2</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 12 ft^2</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Gross rectangular cap area, 12 ft².</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="2" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="PierCap_volume = PierCap_area*PierCap_length to ft^3" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" seplines="False">
                    <expbody>PierCap_volume = PierCap_area*PierCap_length to ft^3</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 230 ft^3</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Gross cap concrete, 230 ft³; no pile deductions, walls or pedestals.</paragraph>
            <embed spacingbefore="8" spacingafter="12" leftindent="0">
                <table name="PierCurrentStations" capture="False" colwidths="1:50, 2:170, 3:170, 4:170">
                    <stylerule range="A1:D5" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.7, &quot;#6A9075&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#6A9075&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenColumns&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#6A9075&quot;);" vertalign="Center" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:D1" background="#DCECE0" fontweight="bold" />
                    <stylerule range="A2:D5" background="#EFF7F1" />
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Pile</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Center from cap end</textvalue></c>
                        <textcell capture="False">
                            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="3">Face nearest left end</paragraph>
                        </textcell>
                        <textcell capture="False">
                            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="3">Face nearest right end</paragraph>
                        </textcell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>1</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PierCap_endCenter+0*Pile_spacing to in"><num>25 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PierCap_endCenter+0*Pile_spacing-Pier_pile_diameter/2 to in"><num>15 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PierCap_endCenter+0*Pile_spacing+Pier_pile_diameter/2 to in"><num>35 in</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>2</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PierCap_endCenter+1*Pile_spacing to in"><num>85 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PierCap_endCenter+1*Pile_spacing-Pier_pile_diameter/2 to in"><num>75 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PierCap_endCenter+1*Pile_spacing+Pier_pile_diameter/2 to in"><num>95 in</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>3</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PierCap_endCenter+2*Pile_spacing to in"><num>145 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PierCap_endCenter+2*Pile_spacing-Pier_pile_diameter/2 to in"><num>135 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PierCap_endCenter+2*Pile_spacing+Pier_pile_diameter/2 to in"><num>155 in</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>4</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PierCap_endCenter+3*Pile_spacing to in"><num>205 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PierCap_endCenter+3*Pile_spacing-Pier_pile_diameter/2 to in"><num>195 in</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PierCap_endCenter+3*Pile_spacing+Pier_pile_diameter/2 to in"><num>215 in</num></c>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">Model cap X coordinates run from -25 to +205 in relative to the first pile center. Add 25 in for cap-end stations. Bearing cap nodes 16/33 at X = 38.50/141.49 in therefore lie at 63.50/166.49 in from the cap end. Separation 102.99 in agrees with the journal’s 103 in to printed XML precision. The earlier model had a 0.36-in right-row offset conflict. The replacement report identifies Pier_Fixed.XML; its bearing offsets remain unverified until that exact XML is supplied.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7">
                <link address="#FBMPPier.PierSourceModelRecord">Report and matching model source; bearing offset review</link>
            </paragraph>
        </section>
    </report>
