                    </row>
                </table>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">Entry axes follow the blue arrows. Node positions are fixed; the coordinate and entry tables rotate together. Moments use the right-hand rule about the chosen axes. Map T/L/V to the actual FBMP X/Y/Z directions.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="8" leftindent="0" background="#FFF8E9">The node labels above are the user-specified map. Member connectivity, global-axis mapping, and the actual node elevation must agree with the model.</paragraph>
            <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="10" leftindent="0">
                <table name="FEWindRegister" title="FEWindRegister" capture="False" colwidths="1:70, 2:80, 3:100, 4:350">
                    <stylerule range="A1:D4" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9.5" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.7, &quot;#7189A6&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#CCD6D0&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenColumns&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#CCD6D0&quot;);" horzalign="Center" vertalign="Center" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:D1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold" />
                    <stylerule range="A2:D4" background="#F1F5FA" />
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Entry case</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>BPAD set</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Limit state</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Concurrent wind pattern</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W1</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>III-S</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Strength III</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Transverse + longitudinal; no direct deck uplift</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W2</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>III-U</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Strength III</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Transverse + deck uplift; no longitudinal force</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W3</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>SI-S</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Service I</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Transverse + longitudinal; no direct deck uplift</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="8" leftindent="0" background="#F1F5FA">ACTIVE PIER WIND SETS: W1 / III-S, W2 / III-U, and W3 / SI-S. Service IV (former W4) is not used for the current pier; it is excluded from entry rows, combinations, summaries, and checks.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" leftindent="0">W1–W3 retain the agreed project labels. They are not verification of FBMP automatic wind/uplift pairing or automatic combination settings.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="1" spacingafter="0" leftindent="0" spacingbefore="0" pagebreakafter="break"> </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="15" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0" keepwithnext="True" fontweight="bold">DC / PL / W1–W3 — NODE ENTRY TABLE</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" leftindent="0">Forces are in kip. Moments use the selected entry units. Positive components act along the displayed positive axes; physical upward wind is retained when V is reversed.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0" fontweight="bold">
                Moment units:
                <dynexp formula="FE_MomentUnits" style="Result only" mathlayout="off">
                    <expresult>kip-ft</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="8" leftindent="0" background="#F1F5FA">Enter DC and PL once as separate load cases. The W rows contain wind only, including the matching residual node moments. Do not add DC or PL to each W row.</paragraph>
