            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">DC = superstructure dead load at the pad; PL = pedestrian live load. Neither includes the other. Cap/pier-wall self-weight is excluded from these entries because the source assumes FBMP supplies it.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">Cheek-wall/pedestal dead weight and direct cap/wall wind are not in this node-entry table. They are listed separately on the next page to avoid duplication.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">For the opposite wind directions, change the controls and use the recalculated complete sets. Do not multiply an uplift set by -1: deck uplift must remain upward.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">Use the displayed residual moments at the displayed node elevation. Do not also apply the original elevated resultants, per-bearing breakdown components, or C004 two-node condensed moments.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="1" spacingafter="0" leftindent="0" spacingbefore="0" pagebreakafter="break"> </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="15" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0" keepwithnext="True" fontweight="bold">OTHER APPLICATIONS / COMBINATION REFERENCE</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0" keepwithnext="True" fontweight="bold">DIRECT CAP / PIER WIND — SEPARATE FROM B1–B4</paragraph>
            <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="10" leftindent="0">
                <table name="FEDirectPierWind" title="FEDirectPierWind" capture="False" colwidths="1:50, 2:160, 3:95, 4:95, 5:260">
                    <stylerule range="A1:E4" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9.5" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.7, &quot;#6A9075&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#CCD6D0&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenColumns&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#CCD6D0&quot;);" horzalign="Center" vertalign="Center" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:E1" background="#DCECE0" fontweight="bold" />
                    <stylerule range="A2:E4" background="#EFF7F1" />
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Case</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Basis</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>T (kip)</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>L (kip)</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Interpretation</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W1</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Face-normal bounds</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_DirectTBound_W1/FE_U_F"><num>4.368586491667764</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_DirectLBound_W1/FE_U_F"><num>20.932810272574702</num></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Not a simultaneous pair</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W2</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Selected perpendicular case</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_DirectT_W2/FE_U_F"><num>4.368586491667764</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_zeroF/FE_U_F"><num>0</num></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Signed concurrent force</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W3</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Face-normal bounds</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_DirectTBound_W3/FE_U_F"><num>1.242423791616</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_DirectLBound_W3/FE_U_F"><num>5.953280668159999</num></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Not a simultaneous pair</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0" background="#FFF8E9">Apply the total to the actual exposed-face centroid or equivalent wall/cap nodes—not once to the cap and again to the wall. The source does not establish those coordinates; transferred direct-wind moments remain unresolved. W1/W3 also require direction-consistent direct-pier cases.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0" keepwithnext="True" fontweight="bold">ADDITIONAL GRAVITY — NOT INCLUDED IN THE MASTER DC ROWS</paragraph>
            <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="10" leftindent="0">
                <table name="FEAdditionalGravity" title="FEAdditionalGravity" capture="False" colwidths="1:70, 2:70, 3:270, 4:250">
                    <stylerule range="A1:D6" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9.5" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.7, &quot;#6A9075&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#CCD6D0&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenColumns&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#CCD6D0&quot;);" horzalign="Center" vertalign="Center" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:D1" background="#DCECE0" fontweight="bold" />
                    <stylerule range="A2:D6" background="#EFF7F1" />
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Bearing</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Node</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Below-pad DC equivalent (kip)</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>DW (kip)</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>B1</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_Node_B1"><textvalue>1L</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_axisV*(FE_DCbelow_B1/FE_U_F)"><num>2.022658125</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_axisV*(FE_DW_B1/FE_U_F)"><num>0</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>B2</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_Node_B2"><textvalue>2L</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_axisV*(FE_DCbelow_B2/FE_U_F)"><num>2.022658125</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_axisV*(FE_DW_B2/FE_U_F)"><num>0</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>B3</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_Node_B3"><textvalue>1R</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_axisV*(FE_DCbelow_B3/FE_U_F)"><num>2.022658125</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_axisV*(FE_DW_B3/FE_U_F)"><num>0</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>B4</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_Node_B4"><textvalue>2R</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_axisV*(FE_DCbelow_B4/FE_U_F)"><num>2.022658125</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_axisV*(FE_DW_B4/FE_U_F)"><num>0</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>TOTAL</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue></textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_axisV*(FE_TotalDCbelow/FE_U_F)"><num>8.0906325</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_axisV*(FE_TotalDW/FE_U_F)"><num>0</num></c>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0">Both columns are signed V-entry forces in the displayed axis system. Below-pad DC is the lumped cheek-wall/pedestal weight: use actual local weights or equivalent shares once. DW is a separate case.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0" keepwithnext="True" fontweight="bold">SOURCE COMBINATION FACTORS — APPLY AFTER CASE ENTRY</paragraph>
            <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="10" leftindent="0">
                <table name="FECombinationFactors" title="FECombinationFactors" capture="False" colwidths="1:165, 2:70, 3:70, 4:70, 5:185, 6:100">
                    <stylerule range="A1:F6" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9.5" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.7, &quot;#7189A6&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#CCD6D0&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenColumns&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#CCD6D0&quot;);" horzalign="Center" vertalign="Center" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:F1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold" />
                    <stylerule range="A2:F6" background="#F1F5FA" />
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Limit state</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>DC</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>PL</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>DW</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Wind case</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Wind factor</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Strength I max</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γDCmax"><num>1.25</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γPLstrength"><num>1.75</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γDWmax"><num>1.5</num></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>None</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_zeroF/FE_U_F"><num>0</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Strength I min</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γDCmin"><num>0.9</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γPLstrength"><num>1.75</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γDWmin"><num>0.65</num></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>None</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_zeroF/FE_U_F"><num>0</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Strength III max</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γDCmax"><num>1.25</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_zeroF/FE_U_F"><num>0</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γDWmax"><num>1.5</num></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W1 or W2</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γWS"><num>1</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Strength III min</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γDCmin"><num>0.9</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_zeroF/FE_U_F"><num>0</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γDWmin"><num>0.65</num></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W1 or W2</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γWS"><num>1</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Service I</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γservice"><num>1</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γservice"><num>1</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γservice"><num>1</num></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W3</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_γWS"><num>1</num></c>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0">This is the source DC/DW/PL/wind subset, not all project actions. Evaluate applicable maximum/minimum permanent-load patterns and required wind directions. Do not factor an already combined source vertical-load result again.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0" keepwithnext="True" fontweight="bold">ENTRY-TRANSFORMATION CHECKS — NOT MEMBER CAPACITY</paragraph>
            <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="10" leftindent="0">
                <table name="FEEntryChecks" title="FEEntryChecks" capture="False" colwidths="1:100, 2:280, 3:280">
                    <stylerule range="A1:C5" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9.5" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.7, &quot;#7189A6&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#CCD6D0&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenColumns&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#CCD6D0&quot;);" horzalign="Center" vertalign="Center" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:C1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold" />
                    <stylerule range="A2:C5" />
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Case</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Force / gravity preservation</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Moment preservation</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W1</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_CheckF_W1"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_CheckM_W1"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W2</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_CheckF_W2"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_CheckM_W2"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W3</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_CheckF_W3"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_CheckM_W3"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>DC / PL totals</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FE_CheckGravity"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>—</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" leftindent="0">The checks compare mapped entry resultants with the original source resultants, including coordinate handedness. They do not verify the actual .in file, automatic combinations, restraints, or structural resistance.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0">
                <link address="#FBMPPier.FourBearingNodeLoads;paragraphfourbearingloads">Source decomposition and original bearing/axis convention</link>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="7" leftindent="0">
                <link address="#CodeReferencesGeneral.CodePage14;paragraphprojectcoderef14General">LRFD load-factor reference retained in the journal</link>
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph />
        <paragraph />
        <paragraph />
        <paragraph />
        <section name="FourBearingNodeLoads" capture="False" hide="true">
            <heading level="0" id="paragraphfourbearingloads">SOURCE DECOMPOSITION — ORIGINAL BEARING LABELS / T0 AXIS</heading>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">SOURCE BASIS ONLY: T0 is the original transverse direction; L points from End Bent 1 to End Bent 2; V0 is upward. The source tuple (T0,L,V0) is right-handed. B-suffixes in NB_* and PedBridgeWeights_2Beams remain original source positions. Use the live FBMP Entry Reference for current bearing/node labels, reversed T, and downward-positive V.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" background="#FFF8E9">CURRENT-TO-SOURCE MAP: current B1 uses source B2; current B2 uses source B1; current B3 uses source B4; current B4 uses source B3. Source tables and raster sketches below are not additional FBMP inputs.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" background="#FFF8E9" fontweight="bold">Model geometry uses the single 36-in cap depth, 6-in pedestal and Type F pad. The notebook pier beam soffit supplies the common reference; cap elevation follows the support stack. Confirm individual seat elevations, separate plates and the actual restraint load path before final model application.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">
                <link address="#SuperstructureUplift">Bearing/cap datum check</link>
            </paragraph>
            <embed spacingafter="12">
                <canvas name="NBFourBearingPlan" title="Four bearing positions at pier" unit="in" size="6.5 in; 2.9 in; scaletofit">
                    <include target="Library.Geometry" />
                    <lines pts="1.0,.6,0;5.5,.6,0;5.5,2.25,0;1.0,2.25,0;1.0,.6,0" linecolor="#444444" linethickness="0.8" />
                    <lines pts="1.0,1.425,0;5.5,1.425,0" linecolor="#AAB6C1" linethickness="0.8" />
                    <lines pts="1.7799999999999998,0.9500000000000001,0;2.02,0.9500000000000001,0;2.02,1.1500000000000001,0;1.7799999999999998,1.1500000000000001,0;1.7799999999999998,0.9500000000000001,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="0.8" />
                    <planecontainer origin="2.1,1.02,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>B1</textvalue></planecontainer>
                    <lines pts="4.4799999999999995,0.9500000000000001,0;4.72,0.9500000000000001,0;4.72,1.1500000000000001,0;4.4799999999999995,1.1500000000000001,0;4.4799999999999995,0.9500000000000001,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="0.8" />
                    <planecontainer origin="4.8,1.02,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>B2</textvalue></planecontainer>
                    <lines pts="1.7799999999999998,1.7,0;2.02,1.7,0;2.02,1.9000000000000001,0;1.7799999999999998,1.9000000000000001,0;1.7799999999999998,1.7,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="0.8" />
                    <planecontainer origin="2.1,1.77,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>B3</textvalue></planecontainer>
                    <lines pts="4.4799999999999995,1.7,0;4.72,1.7,0;4.72,1.9000000000000001,0;4.4799999999999995,1.9000000000000001,0;4.4799999999999995,1.7,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="0.8" />
                    <planecontainer origin="4.8,1.77,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>B4</textvalue></planecontainer>
                    <planecontainer origin="1.0,2.55,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>PLAN — physical bearing rows; dimensions are live; not to scale</textvalue></planecontainer>
                    <planecontainer origin="2.45,1.13,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Span 1 / −L</textvalue></planecontainer>
                    <planecontainer origin="2.45,1.92,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Span 2 / +L</textvalue></planecontainer>
                    <planecontainer origin="1.55,0.28,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>B− beam line</textvalue></planecontainer>
                    <planecontainer origin="4.22,0.28,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>B+ beam line</textvalue></planecontainer>
                    <arrowlines pts="5.92,1.0,0;5.92,2.1,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="0.8" endarrow="6; 3" />
                    <planecontainer origin="5.75,2.27,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>+L</textvalue></planecontainer>
                    <arrowlines pts="3.0,.10,0;3.95,.10,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="0.8" endarrow="6; 3" />
                    <planecontainer origin="3.98,0.05,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>+T</textvalue></planecontainer>
                    <lineardim startpoint="1.9,2.25,0" endpoint="4.6,2.25,0" pointondimline="3.25,2.38,0" formula="BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Beam_spacing" linecolor="#1766A0" textcolor="#1766A0" fontsize="8"><num>8 ft 7 in</num></lineardim>
                </canvas>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_s = BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Beam_spacing to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_s = BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Beam_spacing to ft in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 8 ft 7 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Transverse spacing between bearing lines.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_k = BridgeGeometry_2Beam.PierCL_bearingCL to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_k = BridgeGeometry_2Beam.PierCL_bearingCL to ft in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 0 ft 10.5 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Longitudinal distance from pier centerline to each bearing row.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_zb = BridgeGeometry_2Beam.BearingPlane_CapCG to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_zb = BridgeGeometry_2Beam.BearingPlane_CapCG to ft in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 2 ft 2.562 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Bearing plane above cap centroid, derived from the cap depth and support buildup.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_zn = -FE_NodeElevation" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_zn = -FE_NodeElevation</expbody>
                    <expresult> = -0 ft</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Positive-upward source node elevation, derived from the downward-positive entry V coordinate.</paragraph>
            <section name="NBNote_NB_zn" capture="False" hide="true">
                <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">NB_zn is the positive-upward source elevation, equal to the negative of the entry-node V coordinate. Set FE_NodeElevation in the FBMP Entry Reference: negative entries place nodes above the cap centroid. Separate-node heights require individual transfer equations.</paragraph>
            </section>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_signT = -FE_signT" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_signT = -FE_signT</expbody>
                    <expresult> = -1</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Source-axis wind sign, derived from the current entry T-direction control.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_signL = FE_signL" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_signL = FE_signL</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 1</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Longitudinal wind sign, derived from the current entry direction control.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_zc = BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Dist_windSuperCG_CapCG to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_zc = BridgeGeometry_2Beam.Dist_windSuperCG_CapCG to ft in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 5 ft 9.062 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Concrete wind centroid above cap reference.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_zf = FenceWind.z_eff to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_zf = FenceWind.z_eff to ft in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 14 ft 1.719 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Fence wind centroid above cap reference.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_hc = NB_zc-NB_zb to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_hc = NB_zc-NB_zb to ft in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 3 ft 6.5 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Concrete wind arm above the bearing plane.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_hf = NB_zf-NB_zb to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_hf = NB_zf-NB_zb to ft in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 11 ft 11.156 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Fence wind arm above the bearing plane.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_e = C001WindLoadOnPedBridgeSuperstructure.e_V to ft in" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_e = C001WindLoadOnPedBridgeSuperstructure.e_V to ft in</expbody>
                    <expresult> = 3 ft 4.75 in</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Upward deck-wind eccentricity toward the windward quarter point.</paragraph>
            <section name="NBRepeatedDefinitions" capture="False" hide="true">
