            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">DC cap node includes the entered cheek-wall/pedestal weight as four equal equivalent shares. Cap and pier-wall weight remain excluded because FBMP supplies their self-weight. For local cap design, apply DC pad at B1–B4 and apply cheek-wall/pedestal weight separately at its actual location instead of using the lumped DC cap node column.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" keepwithnext="True">UNEQUAL SPAN EFFECT</paragraph>
            <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="12">
                <table name="NBGravityImbalance" capture="False" colwidths="1:260.0, 2:260.0">
                    <stylerule range="A1:B3" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#6A9075&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.3, &quot;#BCD0C1&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenColumns&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.3, &quot;#BCD0C1&quot;);" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:B1" background="#DCECE0" fontweight="bold" />
                    <stylerule range="A2:B3" background="#EFF7F1" />
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Quantity</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Value</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Span 1 row minus Span 2 row, DC</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PedBridgeWeights_2Beams.ΔDC_rows"><num>4.202476833333037 kip</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Gravity pitch at pier center, M_T</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="PedBridgeWeights_2Beams.MT_DC_pier"><num>3.677167229166407 kip*ft</num></c>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </embed>
            <heading level="1">Wind components and equivalent cap-node actions</heading>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">C002 supplies the simplified horizontal cases. C001 and C004 supply the perpendicular horizontal-plus-uplift cases. Each case below is separate; do not add a simplified case to an uplift case. The prescribed fence pressure remains unchanged between limit states. Horizontal shear sharing is equal between the two beam lines within each span and proportional to the separate span tributaries, retaining the source load-path assumption.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">
                <link address="#CodeReferencesGeneral.CodePage11;paragraphprojectcoderef11General">LRFD 3.8.2 — Strength III upward wind with concurrent perpendicular horizontal wind</link>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">
                <link address="#CodeReferencesGeneral.CodePage14;paragraphprojectcoderef14General">LRFD Table 3.4.1-1 — matching limit-state factors</link>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" keepwithnext="True">WIND CASE REGISTER — WS = 1.0</paragraph>
            <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="12">
                <table name="NBCaseDefinitions" capture="False" colwidths="1:65, 2:175, 3:100, 4:180">
                    <stylerule range="A1:D4" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#6A9075&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.3, &quot;#BCD0C1&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenColumns&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.3, &quot;#BCD0C1&quot;);" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:D1" background="#DCECE0" fontweight="bold" />
                    <stylerule range="A2:D4" background="#EFF7F1" />
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Case</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Concrete source</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Long. / trans.</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Deck uplift</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>III-S</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>C002 Strength III</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>0.25</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>None; simplified case</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>SI-S</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>C002 Service I</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>0.25</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>None</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>III-U</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>C004 Strength III</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>0</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>C001 Strength III</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">For III-S and SI-S evaluate sign pairs (+,+), (+,−), (−,+), (−,−). For III-U evaluate both transverse signs; longitudinal force is zero. The tables show the selected signs live. They are concurrent load sets, not independent component envelopes.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_H(w,l) = w*l/2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_H(w,l) = w*l/2</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Horizontal force delivered to one bearing position; derived equilibrium.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_roll(w,h,l) = w*h*l/NB_s" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_roll(w,h,l) = w*h*l/NB_s</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Compression increment magnitude from transverse overturning.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_lift(w,l) = -w*l/2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_lift(w,l) = -w*l/2</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Uniform upward wind expressed as a downward-load increment.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="5" keepwithnext="True">
                <dynexp formula="NB_ecc(w,l) = w*NB_e*l/NB_s" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False">
                    <expbody>NB_ecc(w,l) = w*NB_e*l/NB_s</expbody>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">Compression increment from windward-quarter-point uplift eccentricity.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">A transverse overturning couple is represented by unequal vertical bearing forces. The remaining roll couple at each cap node is the transverse force times the distance from the node elevation to the bearing plane. Longitudinal source moments are retained as equivalent cap-node pitch couples; they are not individual elastomeric-pad moment demands. A verified restraint model is needed to resolve that longitudinal action into physical pad forces.</paragraph>
            <heading level="2">III-S — selected concurrent wind case</heading>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" keepwithnext="True">PER-BEARING BREAKDOWN — ΔN POSITIVE DOWNWARD</paragraph>
            <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="12">
                <table name="NBComponentsIIIS" capture="False" colwidths="1:176, 2:86, 3:86, 4:86, 5:86">
                    <stylerule range="A1:E9" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#6A9075&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.3, &quot;#BCD0C1&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenColumns&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.3, &quot;#BCD0C1&quot;);" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:E1" background="#DCECE0" fontweight="bold" />
                    <stylerule range="A2:E9" background="#EFF7F1" />
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Component (kip)</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>B1</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>B2</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>B3</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>B4</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Concrete transverse</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HTc_IIIS_1"><num>-9.2650814107366 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HTc_IIIS_2"><num>-9.2650814107366 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HTc_IIIS_3"><num>-9.053628691069129 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HTc_IIIS_4"><num>-9.053628691069129 kip</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Fence transverse</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HTf_IIIS_1"><num>-3.9019208984374956 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HTf_IIIS_2"><num>-3.9019208984374956 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HTf_IIIS_3"><num>-3.812869140625002 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HTf_IIIS_4"><num>-3.812869140625002 kip</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Concrete longitudinal</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HLc_IIIS_1"><num>2.31627035268415 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HLc_IIIS_2"><num>2.31627035268415 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HLc_IIIS_3"><num>2.263407172767282 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HLc_IIIS_4"><num>2.263407172767282 kip</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Fence longitudinal</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HLf_IIIS_1"><num>0.9754802246093739 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HLf_IIIS_2"><num>0.9754802246093739 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HLf_IIIS_3"><num>0.9532172851562505 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="NB_HLf_IIIS_4"><num>0.9532172851562505 kip</num></c>
                    </row>
