            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Use both matching force and residual-couple tables once at the listed node coordinates. If the model uses kip-in, multiply each kip-ft moment by 12. The unequal row forces generate their own pitch and yaw; do not add the collapsed-row residuals from C004.</paragraph>
            <heading level="1">Load factors and combined vertical node loads</heading>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Basis: LRFD Tables 3.4.1-1 and 3.4.1-2, 10th Edition (2024). Maximum/minimum permanent-load factors apply according to whether the force effect increases or reduces the demand. The rows are a gravity/wind subset; mixed stabilizing and destabilizing permanent-load patterns may also govern.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" keepwithnext="True">GRAVITY/WIND SUBSET OF THE MODEL COMBINATIONS</paragraph>
