            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">For manual application of a combined row, use F_V = −N and the matching wind force/couple tables. Do not factor these combined values again. When using FBMP load-combination factors, enter the separate unfactored gravity and matching wind cases instead.</paragraph>
            <heading level="1">Direct wind on the pier — separate application</heading>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Direct cap/wall wind does not pass through the bearings and is not included in B1–B4. The following face-normal forces are source-model component bounds, not one simultaneous full-force pair. The simplified case requires direction-consistent direct-pier loads; the 25% superstructure rule is not a direction-angle definition for the wall.</paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" keepwithnext="True">DIRECT-PIER WIND BOUNDS — KIP</paragraph>
            <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="12">
                <table name="NBDirectWind" capture="False" colwidths="1:173.33333333333334, 2:173.33333333333334, 3:173.33333333333334">
                    <stylerule range="A1:C3" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#6A9075&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.3, &quot;#BCD0C1&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenColumns&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.3, &quot;#BCD0C1&quot;);" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:C1" background="#DCECE0" fontweight="bold" />
                    <stylerule range="A2:C3" background="#EFF7F1" />
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Limit state</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Full face-normal T</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Full face-normal L</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Strength III</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FenceWind.F_wall_T_III"><num>4.368586491667764 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FenceWind.F_wall_L_III"><num>20.932810272574702 kip</num></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Service I</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FenceWind.F_wall_T_SI"><num>1.242423791616 kip</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="FenceWind.F_wall_L_SI"><num>5.953280668159999 kip</num></c>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">For the perpendicular III-U case, pair the signed T direct-pier force with that case, applied at the exposed-face centroid. The idealized L face is parallel to that wind. Actual face-centroid elevations and model wall nodes are not documented by the current four-bearing geometry; complete that separate wall-node mapping before final model loading.</paragraph>
            <heading level="1">Force and moment equilibrium</heading>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" keepwithnext="True">FOUR-NODE EQUILIBRIUM CHECKS</paragraph>
