                </row>
            </table>
        </embed>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">
            <link address="#FBMPPier.FBMPEntryReference">Source pier entry and full decomposition</link>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">
            <link address="#PedBridgeWeights_2Beams">Gravity source: current two-beam weight sheet</link>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">
            <link address="#LoadCombinations">Load-combination applicability notes</link>
        </paragraph>
        <heading level="1" keepwithnext="True">Calculation basis</heading>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">For each bearing, horizontal force = line load × selected span / 4. The transverse bearing couple uses the wind heights above the bearing plane and the windward-quarter-point uplift eccentricity. Direct uplift = −uplift line load × span / 4. Residual moments transfer to the actual node elevation and longitudinal location: ΔM_T = ΔL·F_V and ΔM_V = −ΔL·F_T. Gravity receives the same ΔL·F_V transfer. The resultant checks sum r × F + M at the application nodes about the centered cap/pile line.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" leftindent="0">Source: supplied journal (34), former §5.3 Entry Reference - Pier; C001, C002, C004, current geometry and quantity modules. No FBMP .in file was edited or verified. The largest span is selected live; if span 2 becomes longer, the node-assignment status explicitly requests remapping.</paragraph>
        <section name="EBOffsetResultants" capture="False" hide="false">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0">ECCENTRICITY — RESULTANTS ABOUT THE CENTERED PILE/CAP LINE</paragraph>
            <embed spacingafter="9">
                <table name="EBOffsetTotals" capture="False" colwidths="1:60, 2:130, 3:130, 4:130, 5:130">
                    <stylerule range="A1:E6" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9.5" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.5, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:E1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold" />
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Case</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>T moment</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>L moment</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>V moment</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>Equilibrium</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>DC</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_SumMT_DC/EB_U_M"><num>46.034274291666634</num></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>0</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>0</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_CheckOffset_DC"><textvalue>PASS</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>PL</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_SumMT_PL/EB_U_M"><num>14.492249999999988</num></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>0</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>0</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_CheckOffset_PL"><textvalue>PASS</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W1</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_SumMT_W1/EB_U_M"><num>-54.25411760044521</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_SumML_W1/EB_U_M"><num>-217.01647040178085</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_SumMV_W1/EB_U_M"><num>-6.583501154587047</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_CheckM_W1"><textvalue>PASS</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W2</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_SumMT_W2/EB_U_M"><num>-3.645427083333331</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_SumML_W2/EB_U_M"><num>-266.5335216170586</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_SumMV_W2/EB_U_M"><num>-6.583501154587049</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_CheckM_W2"><textvalue>PASS</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <c capture="False"><textvalue>W3</textvalue></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_SumMT_W3/EB_U_M"><num>-35.17532302796966</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_SumML_W3/EB_U_M"><num>-140.70129211187864</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_SumMV_W3/EB_U_M"><num>-3.268452685885414</num></c>
                        <c capture="False" formula="EB_CheckM_W3"><textvalue>PASS</textvalue></c>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </embed>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">These are whole-end-bent resultants for checking the load set. They are not extra nodal loads. Units follow the moment-entry selector. Pile reactions require the foundation model; the bearing compression screen does not rule out pile tension or a controlling W2 foundation case.</paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" background="#F1F5FA">Revision — 30 September 2026: the pile line is centered in the cap width; bearings have a geometry-derived longitudinal eccentricity. Bearing location and application-node location are separate. Wind and gravity force magnitudes are unchanged; residual moments and whole-cap resultants now include that offset.</paragraph>
        <section name="EBCurrentDesignRecord" capture="False" hide="false">
            <heading level="0" keepwithnext="True" pagebreakbefore="break">Current end-bent cap design record — 8 October 2026</heading>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" leftindent="0" spacingafter="7" background="#FFF8E9">Block 2 (longitudinal reinforcement) is live from CapDesignEndBentOne, the 19 October 2026 case selected under D-051. Blocks 1 and 3 remain the 8 October record pending refresh.</paragraph>
            <embed spacingbefore="8" spacingafter="12" leftindent="0">
                <table name="EBDesignRecordContext" capture="False" colwidths="1:110, 2:410">
                    <stylerule range="A1:B5" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.7, &quot;#7189A6&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#7189A6&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenColumns&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.35, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);" vertalign="Center" />
                    <stylerule range="A1:B1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold" />
                    <stylerule range="A2:B5" background="#F1F5FA" />
