        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#A64A20">Mirror pile moments reverse sign across the wall center. Add these actions only when they replace the existing equivalent wall-load application; do not add the same wall weight twice in FBMP. Local pipe-shell checks require the concurrent bridge axial/bending state and the effective pipe thickness shown in Step 1.</paragraph>
        <section name="C006Work08" capture="False" hide="false">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="12" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#1766A0" texthighlight="#EDF3F8" id="c006work08" keepwithnext="True" pagebreakbefore="break" fontweight="bold">
                <link address="#PierWallFins.C006Strategy08;c006strategy08">STEP 8 OF 8 | Design summary and verification boundaries</link>
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <section name="C006CheckCollector" capture="False" hide="true">
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">
                <dynexp formula="C006_Checks = [Chk_reactions, Chk_model, Chk_saddle, Chk_hairpin, Chk_development, Chk_bend, Chk_plate_flex, Chk_plate_shear, Chk_plate_VM, Chk_root, Chk_strip_flex, Chk_strip_shear, Chk_service, Chk_ST, Chk_STMgrid, Chk_spacing, Chk_fit, Chk_joints]" mathlayout="on" showsteps="false">
                    <expbody>C006_Checks = [Chk_reactions, Chk_model, Chk_saddle, Chk_hairpin, Chk_development, Chk_bend, Chk_plate_flex, Chk_plate_shear, Chk_plate_VM, Chk_root, Chk_strip_flex, Chk_strip_shear, Chk_service, Chk_ST, Chk_STMgrid, Chk_spacing, Chk_fit, Chk_joints]</expbody>
                    <expresult> = [✓ PASS, ✓ PASS, ✓ PASS, ...]</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5">
                <dynexp formula="Status_numeric = If(Any(C006_Checks, ==&quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;), &quot;⊗ There are FAILURES&quot;, &quot;✓ All Checks Pass&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showsteps="false">
                    <expbody>Status_numeric = If(Any(C006_Checks, =="⊗ FAIL"), "⊗ There are FAILURES", "✓ All Checks Pass")</expbody>
                    <expresult> = ✓ All Checks Pass</expresult>
                </dynexp>
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="Local_node_complete = false" mathlayout="on" showsteps="false" seplines="false" style="Required Input">
                <expbody>Local_node_complete = false</expbody>
                <expresult> = False</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Local hanger/concrete/saddle load-transfer mechanism independently completed?</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="Local_pipe_complete = false" mathlayout="on" showsteps="false" seplines="false" style="Required Input">
                <expbody>Local_pipe_complete = false</expbody>
                <expresult> = False</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Local pipe-shell and concurrent global pile verification independently completed?</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="Geometry_confirmed = false" mathlayout="on" showsteps="false" seplines="false" style="Required Input">
                <expbody>Geometry_confirmed = false</expbody>
                <expresult> = False</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Source wall-bottom elevation, cover/environment, and required pile-position envelope confirmed?</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="0" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
            <dynexp formula="Status_C006 = If(Status_numeric==&quot;⊗ There are FAILURES&quot;,&quot;REVISE — NUMERICAL CHECK FAILS&quot;,If(And(Local_node_complete,Local_pipe_complete,Geometry_confirmed),&quot;CHECKS PASS — WELD CHECK SEPARATE&quot;,&quot;PROVISIONAL — LOCAL CHECKS OPEN&quot;))" mathlayout="on" showsteps="false" seplines="false" style="Result only" showformula="false" showidentifier="false" showresult="true">
                <expresult>PROVISIONAL — LOCAL CHECKS OPEN</expresult>
            </dynexp>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">Live module status; separate weld calculation remains required.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="5" keepwithnext="True" fontweight="bold">Implemented numerical checks</paragraph>
        <embed spacingafter="10">
            <table name="C006Table289" title="Implemented numerical checks" capture="False" colwidths="1:490, 2:160">
                <stylerule range="A1:B19" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.5, &quot;#6A9075&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.3, &quot;#BCCEC0&quot;);" />
                <stylerule range="A1:B1" background="#DCECE0" fontweight="bold" />
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Check</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Result</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Six wall reactions reproduce the gross wall weight.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_reactions"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Validity of the symmetric four-pile/six-fin reaction model.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_model"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Selected saddle and hairpin force points fit on the fin projection.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_saddle"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Hairpin tensile resistance under assigned actual gravity loads.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_hairpin"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Available straight-tail length exceeds the full-yield requirement.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_development"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Hairpin inside bend diameter satisfies the general #5 bar minimum.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_bend"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Selected fin satisfies adopted biaxial elastic/LTB resistance.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_plate_flex"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Selected fin satisfies root shear yielding and rupture.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_plate_shear"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Selected fin passes additional conservative combined-stress screen.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_plate_VM"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Plate geometry remains valid and inside the source wall.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_root"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Wind-strip flexure and minimum flexural reinforcement.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_strip_flex"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Wind-strip shear and transverse reinforcement area/spacing.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_strip_shear"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Supplementary Service I cracked-section check with FDOT amendment.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_service"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Shrinkage/temperature steel and maximum spacing, both directions and faces.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_ST"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Adopted disturbed-region grid area and twelve-inch ceiling.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_STMgrid"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>General grid clear spacing and selected cross-tie spacing.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_spacing"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Selected trial layout fits only within the specified pile-position envelope.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_fit"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False"><textvalue>Wall length does not require an intermediate joint under the 30-foot screen.</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Chk_joints"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
            </table>
        </embed>
        <embed spacingbefore="6" spacingafter="10">
            <table name="C006Box290" capture="False" colwidths="1:650">
                <stylerule range="A1:A6" background="#F1F5FA" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);" />
                <stylerule range="A1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold" />
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box290R0" capture="False">
                        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">EXPLICIT COMPLETION ITEMS — NOT INCLUDED IN AN OVERALL PASS</paragraph>
                    </textcell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box290R1" capture="False">
                        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">1. Local node and wall gravity collection: substantiate the reserved transfer zone, actual struts/nodes, splitting confinement, bar development beyond the relevant separation surfaces, and the round saddle contact/retention detail.</paragraph>
                    </textcell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box290R2" capture="False">
                        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">2. Receiving pipe: check localized shell yielding/plastification, punching/tearing and interaction with the actual concurrent pile stress state at the fin elevation. Use the effective pipe wall, not the nominal 5/8-inch wall. No pipe local-resistance pass is claimed here.</paragraph>
                    </textcell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box290R3" capture="False">
                        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">3. Geometry: confirm source wall-bottom elevation, environmental cover and the tighter wall-region position tolerance. The old source wall quantity has not been silently changed.</paragraph>
                    </textcell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box290R4" capture="False">
                        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">4. Weld: use the exported root cases in the separate weld calculation, including relocation to the actual weld centroid and adjacent base-metal failure paths. No weld design is contained in C006.</paragraph>
                    </textcell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box290R5" capture="False">
                        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">5. Preserve external applicability decisions for collision, seismic, construction and fatigue; resolve differential pile movement/cap-wall restraint consistently with the full substructure model. The one-foot wind strip is not a coupled pier model.</paragraph>
                    </textcell>
                </row>
            </table>
        </embed>
        <embed spacingbefore="6" spacingafter="10">
            <table name="C006Box291" capture="False" colwidths="1:650">
                <stylerule range="A1:A4" background="#F1F5FA" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);" />
                <stylerule range="A1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold" />
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box291R0" capture="False">
                        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">SELECTED TRIAL DETAIL</paragraph>
                    </textcell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box291R1" capture="False">
                        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">One upper row; six inward/opposed fin plates total. Two designated #5 hairpins over a round bearing saddle at each fin. Fin and hairpin dimensions remain live in the tables.</paragraph>
                    </textcell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box291R2" capture="False">
                        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Fin-root actions are exported in local right-handed axes with +z downward. Each HY row is a separate connection-development target, not a global bridge load combination.</paragraph>
                    </textcell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box291R3" capture="False">
                        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Drawings must identify the selected one-row arrangement, the fin/root reference, the designated hairpins, the fitted saddle and the retained source geometry. Local checks listed above must be completed before release.</paragraph>
                    </textcell>
                </row>
            </table>
        </embed>
    </report>
