        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">Positive extra setback is the outward parallel-move shortfall. Side rows compare only the specified 24-inch clearance; they are not strap feasibility results.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" pagebreakbefore="break">4. END BENT 2 — FRONT AND SIDE PLAN</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">Red open boundary shows computed front and specified side offsets. There is no rear-wall criterion. Gray is the cap; black is the current back of facing. Local x runs across the piles and +y into the approach.</paragraph>
