        </embed>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">Positive extra setback is the outward parallel-move shortfall. Side rows compare only the specified 24-inch clearance; they are not strap feasibility results.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" pagebreakbefore="break">5. SEPARATE REQUIREMENTS AND USE</paragraph>
        <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="8">
            <table name="CapSetback" capture="False" colwidths="1:290, 2:120, 3:120">
                <stylerule range="A1:C3" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#A7B9C6&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.4, &quot;#CBD5DD&quot;);" />
                <row>
                    <c capture="False" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"><textvalue>Separate front-cap check</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"><textvalue>End Bent 1</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"><textvalue>End Bent 2</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><textvalue>Front cap face to back of front facing</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" background="#EFF7F1" formula="Bent1CapGap to in"><num>25.18166040529446 in</num></c>
                    <c capture="False" background="#EFF7F1" formula="Bent2CapGap to in"><num>24.616880361260698 in</num></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><textvalue>SDG 3.13.2.N.2.i: 24 in minimum</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Bent1CapStatus"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="Bent2CapStatus"><textvalue>✓ PASS</textvalue></c>
                </row>
            </table>
        </embed>
        <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="8">
            <table name="SkewBasis" capture="False" colwidths="1:290, 2:240">
                <stylerule range="A1:B2" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#A7B9C6&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.4, &quot;#CBD5DD&quot;);" />
                <row>
                    <c capture="False" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"><textvalue>Front skew basis</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"><textvalue>Live result</textvalue></c>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <c capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><textvalue>SDG 3.13.2.K.8 ordinary plan skew</textvalue></c>
                    <c capture="False" formula="SkewStatus"><textvalue>Within ordinary 15 deg limit</textvalue></c>
                </row>
            </table>
        </embed>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Front strap clearance and cap-to-facing clearance are separate measurements. Keep the front face of the cap at least 24 inches from the back of facing. The cap is shown in plan for coordination; no elevation strap/cap clearance is solved here.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">The side-wall 24-inch pile-face offset is the specified layout criterion for this task. SDG 3.13.2.N.2.i applies 24 inches to cap/front-facing clearance; N.2.ii applies it to battered pile/leveling-pad clearance. Those provisions are not a side-wall strap-clearance calculation.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Pile placement tolerance is excluded as requested. Skew may be reversed around the nominal pile, but this does not demonstrate clearance for all possible as-built positions or the full reinforcement route. Coordinate actual pile positions and adjacent obstructions separately.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Only the front wall is checked for nominal centered-strap geometry. Side reinforcement, rear walls, elevation routing, reinforcement length, connection/development and wall stability are outside this module. No side or overall wall-design pass is implied.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">The plan assumes wall faces parallel to these axes. Nominal pile width defines the clearance; the tiny saved frame rotation is retained for pile centers and the cap outline. The open boundary has no rear edge or rear-wall requirement.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">SOURCE AND PROVENANCE</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">Shared pile and cap dimensions: BridgeGeometry_2Beam. Current MSE wall back-face lines: saved FreeCAD model, project_current\geometry\freecad\B4 Pedestrian Bridge and Ramps - Pond14D - Source Update 20261010.FCStd. Facing thickness projects outward from the profile.</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="6">Saved model SHA-256: 7368774487c1456238df13c80e33ddf3871907982ff91938e1ae1b4eebf52676</paragraph>
        <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">
            <link address="https://www.fdot.gov/Structures/StructuresManual/CurrentRelease">FDOT Structures Manual, January 2026 — SDG 3.13.2.K.8 and N.2.</link>
        </paragraph>
    </report>
