  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="16" spacingafter="2" fontweight="bold">D2 I-95 PEDESTRIAN BRIDGE</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">End Bent 2 — Distilled Cap Design Calculation</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Project: D2 I-95 Pedestrian Bridge.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Distilled from End Bent 2 Cap Design 10-19.html (generated 2026-10-19T14:37:53+00:00); same case (canonical SHA-256 8a08d9d28568) and C005 formula set (327838126d06) as the report; FBMP End Bent 2_Fixed.XML (3543df298b92). Blockpad edition written by scripts/build_cap_bpad.py from the same case; every definition was evaluated independently and compared with the cap tool to 1 part in 10⁹.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Codes: AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specifications, 10th edition (2024); FDOT Structures Design Guidelines, January 2026, 4.1.4A–C; inherited sectional relations of the cap tool (C005 formula set 327838126d06).</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Tool status: CHECK FAILURES — revise the trial cage or section. Inputs are highlighted amber; distilled results are the green tables.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">1. Scope</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Computed here: sectional flexure, minimum steel, strain and Service I crack control in regions N (top steel), P (bottom steel at the piles) and B (bottom steel with the added span bars); the shear depth; actual-cage shear, longitudinal tension, torsion screen and minimum transverse steel at the governing stations found by the tool's station search; the governing transverse spacing; face shrinkage and temperature steel; skin steel; and the governing hook development.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Taken from the tool and not recomputed: the station search itself, the intersected-leg window areas and the developed (credited) steel areas (shown as inputs), the detailing and geometry flags, transverse anchorage, the end grid and the D-regions.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Service III (D-007) and fatigue remain pending.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">2. Inputs</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Shared geometry, materials and factors are live references to the journal; the owner is named beside each.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Geometry and materials</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="b = BridgeGeometry_2Beam.EndBentCap_width to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
