  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Figure 3. Demand/capacity ratio of each distilled check (stems) against the 1.0 limit. The stems are live formulas of the check ratios: a stem turns red when its ratio passes 1.0.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C" background="#F1F5FA">Check numbers: 1 axial compression; 2 axial + biaxial flexure, 5.6.4.5; 3 axial + flexure, resultant axis; 4 shear; 5 tension; 6 Service I compression; 7 Service I tension; 8 effective prestress; 9 driving strength; 10 minimum size; 11 pile spacing; 12 bearing resistance vs Table 3.5.13-1.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C" background="#F1F5FA">The notebook lists 15 PENDING items; the distilled ratios above do not close them: Axial compression · maximum Pu / φPn,max; Axial + biaxial flexure · LRFD Eq. 5.6.4.5-3; Axial + flexure · resultant bending axis (strain compatibility); Shear · general procedure; Service I concrete tension; Minimum square pile size (Table 3.5.1-1); Pile-to-cap moment transfer (embedment below 48 in); Pile Data Table completeness (SDM 11.4); Environment classification; Pile-to-cap connection (12 in embedment); Downdrag source documented; FBMP export current; Minimum tip elevation; Scour resistance and elevations; Drivability.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C" background="#F1F5FA">FB-MultiPier reports a largest model D/C of 0.46 at combo 2 STRENGTH-III · pile 4 · element 12J · EL 18.60 ft. The distilled Status covers the recomputed numerical checks only; it is not design acceptance.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">A distilled result of ✓ covers only the recomputed numerical checks; it is not design acceptance. The pending items of the notebook stay open. Recalculate in Blockpad after any input change.</paragraph>
</report><report name="PileDesignEndBentTwo" title="End Bent 2 Pile Design - Distilled" unit="in" pagesize="816,1056" margin="48,48,48,48" bordermargin="0,0,0,0" collapsemargins="False">
  <include target="Library.Geometry"/>
  <stylerule type="AnyEquation" name="Required Input" texthighlight="#F7E6B9"/>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="16" spacingafter="2" fontweight="bold">D2 I-95 PEDESTRIAN BRIDGE</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">End Bent 2 Pile Design</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Project: D2 I-95 Pedestrian Bridge.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Distilled from the pile design notebook (package 32d46a79afd4), case "End Bent 2 piles: 18 in square prestressed concrete, FBMP fixed run". Same inputs, equations and load combinations as the notebook; results should match its exported report. Blockpad edition written by pile_design/bpad.py (scripts/build_pile_bpad.py) from the same case; every definition was evaluated independently and compared with the notebook to 1 part in 10⁹.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Codes: AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specifications, 10th edition (2024): 5.6.4.4, 5.6.4.5, 5.6.6.1, 5.7.3.3, 5.7.3.4.2, 5.9.2.3.2, 5.12.9.4; FDOT Structures Design Guidelines (SDG) 3.5 and Structures Detailing Manual (SDM) 11.4, January 2026; Standard Plans Index 455.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Status: All numerical checks pass (largest ratio 1.00) · 15 pending item(s) remain. Inputs are highlighted amber; distilled results are the green tables.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">1. Design basis</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• FBMP source: End Bent 2_Fixed.XML, SHA-256 3543df298b92593ce9bac14f9228ffacf5b0ce7e76b5e1d887ae228ef811a90e (registered export EB2-XML). 4 piles at 4.5 ft; cutoff elevation 41.2567 ft, ground 23.59 ft.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Pile: Standard Plans Index 455-018 (18 in square), strand pattern 12~0.6, spiral 0.034 in² wire at 6 in.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Downdrag 18 tons per pile is a drag load DR: gamma_DR = 1.1 (strength) and 1 (Service I) in the structural demands (LRFD Table 3.4.1-1, 10.7.3.7); it is excluded from the Factored Design Load and added nominally to the required bearing resistance (SDG Eq. 3-1, phi = 0.75).</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Every definition was read back from the XML and evaluated by an independent Blockpad-syntax evaluator, then compared with the notebook (and with the Mathcad worksheet) before the file was written. Governing records, the notebook angles, the neutral-axis depth c_gov and the few values found by a search over the interaction sweep are amber inputs read from the notebook.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• The interaction curve of Figure 2 is a picture of the notebook's sweep. The 5.6.4.5 route, the resultant-axis check at c_gov, the demands and every ratio are live formulas.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">2. Inputs</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Pile and layout</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="D_pile = 18 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>D_pile = 18 in</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Pile size (square side, or pipe outside diameter)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="N_pile = 4" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>N_pile = 4</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Piles in the support</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="S_pile = 4.5 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>S_pile = 4.5 ft</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Center-to-center pile spacing</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="EL_cutoff = 41.256667 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>EL_cutoff = 41.256667 ft</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Pile cutoff elevation (FBMP pile head)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="EL_ground = 23.59 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>EL_ground = 23.59 ft</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Ground elevation (top of soil layer 1)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="L_unsupported = 17.666667 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>L_unsupported = 17.666667 ft</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Length above ground (cutoff - ground); editable</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="embed_cap = 12 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>embed_cap = 12 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Pile embedment into the cap</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Loads and geotechnical</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="DD_tons = 18" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>DD_tons = 18</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Downdrag (drag load DR) per pile, short tons [pending confirmation]</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="gamma_DR_str = 1.1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>gamma_DR_str = 1.1</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Drag-load factor, strength limit states (structural)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="gamma_DR_ser = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>gamma_DR_ser = 1</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Drag-load factor, Service I</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="phi_geo = 0.75" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>phi_geo = 0.75</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Geotechnical resistance factor (compression, Davisson)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="R_scour_net_tons = 0" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>R_scour_net_tons = 0</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Net scour resistance, short tons [pending confirmation]</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="R_scour_total_tons = 0" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>R_scour_total_tons = 0</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Total scour resistance, short tons [pending confirmation]</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="K_eff = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>K_eff = 1</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Effective length factor K</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="soil_type = 0" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>soil_type = 0</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Soil for depth to fixity (0 sand, 1 clay) [pending confirmation]</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="n_h = 0.556 ksi/ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>n_h = 0.556 ksi/ft</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Rate of increase of soil modulus, sand</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="S_u = 1 kip/ft^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>S_u = 1 kip/ft^2</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Undrained shear strength, clay (used only for soil type 1) [pending confirmation]</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Environment and policy</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="environment = 2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>environment = 2</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Environment classification [pending confirmation]</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="min_size_policy = 14 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>min_size_policy = 14 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Minimum square pile size, pedestrian bridge</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="λ = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>λ = 1</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Concrete density modification factor</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Prestressed concrete pile</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="fc = 6.5 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>fc = 6.5 ksi</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Pile concrete strength f'c</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="w_c = 0.15 kip/ft^3" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>w_c = 0.15 kip/ft^3</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Concrete unit weight (for Ec)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="K_1 = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>K_1 = 1</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Aggregate correction factor for Ec</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="phi_c = 0.75" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>phi_c = 0.75</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Compression-controlled resistance factor</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="phi_t = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>phi_t = 1</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Tension-controlled resistance factor, bonded prestressing</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="n_sweep = 121" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>n_sweep = 121</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Neutral-axis sweep points for the interaction curve</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Prestress and strand</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="f_pu = 270 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>f_pu = 270 ksi</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Strand ultimate strength (Grade 270 LRS)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="f_py = 243 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>f_py = 243 ksi</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Strand yield strength 0.9 fpu</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="E_p = 28500 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>E_p = 28500 ksi</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Strand modulus</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="loss_frac = 0.2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>loss_frac = 0.2</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Prestress loss as a fraction of the jacking force</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="d_edge = 3.5 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>d_edge = 3.5 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Strand center distance from the pile face</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Shear reinforcement</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="spiral_wire_area = 0.034 in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>spiral_wire_area = 0.034 in^2</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Spiral wire area (one leg)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="spiral_pitch = 6 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>spiral_pitch = 6 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Spiral pitch</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="f_y_spiral = 70 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>f_y_spiral = 70 ksi</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Spiral wire yield strength [pending confirmation]</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="a_g = 0.75 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>a_g = 0.75 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Maximum aggregate size</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="φ_v = 0.9" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>φ_v = 0.9</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Shear resistance factor, concrete</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Standard Plans Index 455-018, strand pattern 12~0.6</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="N_str = 12" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>N_str = 12</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>strands in pattern 12~0.6</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="A_str = 0.217 in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>A_str = 0.217 in^2</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>strand nominal area</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="P_jack = 35 kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>P_jack = 35 kip</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>jacking force per strand, Standard Plans</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="d_void = 0 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>d_void = 0 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>void diameter (Index 455-030 only)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="R_drive_tons = 300" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>R_drive_tons = 300</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">maximum driving resistance, SDG Table 3.5.13-1, tons</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="M_splice = 245 kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>M_splice = 245 kip*ft</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Spec Table 455-2 splice bending strength (INFO)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">3. Demands from the FBMP export</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Governing records of End Bent 2_Fixed.XML for each check (records 1 to 6). FBMP axial force is converted to compression positive. The drag load DR = DD is added to the axial force at every station (LRFD Table 3.4.1-1, 10.7.3.7): gamma_DR for the limit state of the record. Downdrag is not in the Factored Design Load.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Axial: combo 3 STRENGTH-III · pile 4 · element 10J · EL 23.59 ft.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• 5.6.4.5: combo 2 STRENGTH-III · pile 4 · element 12J · EL 18.23 ft (+1 tied).</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Resultant: combo 2 STRENGTH-III · pile 4 · element 13I · EL 18.23 ft.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Shear: combo 3 STRENGTH-III · pile 4 · element 15I · EL 12.87 ft.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Svc comp.: combo 4 SERVICE-I · pile 4 · element 12J · EL 18.23 ft.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Svc tens.: combo 4 SERVICE-I · pile 1 · element 1I · EL 41.26 ft (+239 tied).</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Governing FBMP records, one row per check (inputs read from the export)</paragraph>
  <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="8">
    <table name="DemandInputs" capture="False" colwidths="1:120, 2:88, 3:88, 4:88, 5:88, 6:88">
      <stylerule range="A1:F7" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#A78638&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.4, &quot;#A78638&quot;);"/>
      <stylerule range="A1:F1" horzalign="Center" vertalign="Center"/>
      <stylerule range="B2:F7" horzalign="Center" vertalign="Center"/>
      <row>
        <c capture="False" background="#F7E6B9" fontweight="bold">
          <textvalue>Record</textvalue>
        </c>
        <c capture="False" background="#F7E6B9" fontweight="bold">
          <textvalue>P_fbmp (kip)</textvalue>
        </c>
        <c capture="False" background="#F7E6B9" fontweight="bold">
          <textvalue>M_2 (kip*ft)</textvalue>
        </c>
        <c capture="False" background="#F7E6B9" fontweight="bold">
          <textvalue>M_3 (kip*ft)</textvalue>
        </c>
        <c capture="False" background="#F7E6B9" fontweight="bold">
          <textvalue>M_res (kip*ft)</textvalue>
        </c>
        <c capture="False" background="#F7E6B9" fontweight="bold">
          <textvalue>V_res (kip)</textvalue>
        </c>
      </row>
      <row>
