  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">The strand coordinates are scalars: x_st_1 to x_st_12 and y_st_1 to y_st_12. Strand 1 is written out, strands 2 to 12 are in the collapsed section, and the strand table in Section 9 lists them all.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">6. Axial resistance (LRFD 5.6.4.4, 5.5.4.2)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="P_u_axial = P_u_1 to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>P_u_axial = P_u_1 to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = 144.940 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">largest factored compression incl. drag load</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="P_o = k_c*fc*(A_g - A_ps) - A_ps*(f_pe - E_p*eps_cu) to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>P_o = k_c*fc*(A_g - A_ps) - A_ps*(f_pe - E_p*eps_cu) to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = 1662.355 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">axial resistance at zero eccentricity, 5.6.4.4-2</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="P_n_max = 0.85*P_o to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>P_n_max = 0.85*P_o to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = 1413.002 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">maximum nominal axial resistance (spiral)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="P_r_max = phi_c*P_n_max to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>P_r_max = phi_c*P_n_max to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = 1059.751 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">maximum factored axial resistance</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="phi_Po = phi_c*P_o to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>phi_Po = phi_c*P_o to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = 1246.766 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">phi Po, used in Eq. 5.6.4.5-1</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="P_bi_lim = 0.1*phi_c*fc*A_g to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>P_bi_lim = 0.1*phi_c*fc*A_g to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = 157.950 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">axial load limit between Eqs. 5.6.4.5-1 and -3</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="P_t_yield = A_ps*f_py to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>P_t_yield = A_ps*f_py to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = 632.772 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">strand yield limit Aps fpy (upper bound of tension, 5.6.6.1)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="DC_axial = P_u_axial/P_r_max" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>DC_axial = P_u_axial/P_r_max</expbody>
      <expresult> = 0.137</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">axial compression D/C, largest Pu / phi Pn,max</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" pagebreakbefore="break">7. Interaction by strain compatibility (LRFD 5.6.4.5, C5.6.2.1, 5.5.4.2)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Strain is linear with the extreme compression fiber at eps_cu = 0.003 and a neutral-axis depth c swept geometrically from 4H to 0.02H in the notebook (H = depth of the section normal to the bending axis). Strand strain = eps_pe + eps_ce + eps_cu (d - c)/c.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Strand stress: PCI power formula for Grade 270 low-relaxation strand in tension, Ep eps in compression (no correction for displaced concrete). Concrete: rectangular block a = beta1 c on the compressed part of the square (chamfers ignored).</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Pn is held between -Aps fpy and Pn,max; phi runs from 0.75 to 1.00 as the net tensile strain goes from 0.002 to 0.005. The pure-compression and pure-tension points are scalars below.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Blockpad has no vector variables, so the 121-point sweep is not written as formulas. Figure 2 is a picture of the notebook's sweep. Section 9 evaluates the same equations (strain, power-formula stress, block geometry, Pn, Mn, phi, Pr, Mr) at the single neutral-axis depth c_gov, strand by strand.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="12" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="6" keepwithnext="True">End points of the curve</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="P_r_pc = phi_c*P_n_max to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>P_r_pc = phi_c*P_n_max to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = 1059.751 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">pure compression: phi Pn,max (Mr = 0)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="P_n_pt = -P_t_yield to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>P_n_pt = -P_t_yield to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = -632.772 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">pure tension: Pn = -Aps fpy (Mr = 0)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="P_r_pt = -phi_t*P_t_yield to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>P_r_pt = -phi_t*P_t_yield to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = -632.772 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">pure tension: phi Pn, phi = tension-controlled</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="12" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="6" keepwithnext="True">Bending about an axis parallel to a face (angle 0)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="sn_x = Sin(0 deg)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>sn_x = Sin(0 deg)</expbody>
      <expresult> = 0.000</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">sin of the bending-axis angle</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="cs_x = Sin((0 deg) + (90 deg))" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>cs_x = Sin((0 deg) + (90 deg))</expbody>
      <expresult> = 1.000</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">cos of the bending-axis angle</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="H_x = D_pile*(sn_x + cs_x) to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>H_x = D_pile*(sn_x + cs_x) to in</expbody>
      <expresult> = 18.000 in</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">depth of the section normal to the bending axis</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="s_max_x = H_x/2 to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>s_max_x = H_x/2 to in</expbody>
      <expresult> = 9.000 in</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">centroid to the extreme compression fiber</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="t1_x = D_pile*sn_x to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>t1_x = D_pile*sn_x to in</expbody>
      <expresult> = 0.000 in</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">depth at which the compressed width stops growing</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="t2_x = D_pile*cs_x to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>t2_x = D_pile*cs_x to in</expbody>
      <expresult> = 18.000 in</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">depth at which the compressed width starts to shrink</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="q_x = sn_x*cs_x" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>q_x = sn_x*cs_x</expbody>
      <expresult> = 0.000</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">sin x cos of the angle</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="s_st_x_1 = -sn_x*x_st_1 + cs_x*y_st_1 to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
