    </canvas>
  </embed>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Figure 2. Interaction diagram: factored curves for bending parallel to a face and about the governing resultant axis, the nominal curve (dashed) and the governing demand points. The curves are a picture of the notebook's 121-point sweep and do not move when an input changes; the check at c_gov (Section 9), the demands, the phi Pn,max line and the demand points are live.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">10. Tension (LRFD 5.6.6.1, 5.8.2.4.1-1)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="P_n_t = A_ps*Min(f_py, f_pe + (60 ksi)) to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>P_n_t = A_ps*Min(f_py, f_pe + (60 ksi)) to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = 492.240 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">nominal tension resistance (fy = 60 ksi, no nonprestressed steel)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="P_r_t = phi_t*P_n_t to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>P_r_t = phi_t*P_n_t to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = 492.240 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">factored tension resistance</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="DC_t = T_u/P_r_t" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>DC_t = T_u/P_r_t</expbody>
      <expresult> = 0.000</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">tension D/C, maximum strength uplift</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" pagebreakbefore="break">11. Shear: general procedure (LRFD 5.7.3.3, 5.7.3.4.2)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Governing shear record (record 4). Aps and de are those of the half depth on the flexural tension side of the resultant bending axis (angle alpha_sh from the notebook). Spiral legs crossing the shear plane: two.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="V_u_sh = V_res_4 to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>V_u_sh = V_res_4 to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = 9.261 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">resultant shear</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="M_u_sh = M_res_4 to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>M_u_sh = M_res_4 to kip*ft</expbody>
      <expresult> = 83.007 kip*ft</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">concurrent resultant moment</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="P_u_sh = P_u_4 to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>P_u_sh = P_u_4 to kip</expbody>
      <expresult> = 131.930 kip</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">factored axial load</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="alpha_sh = 1.712079533854103 deg" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input">
      <expbody>alpha_sh = 1.712079533854103 deg</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">bending-axis angle of the shear record, from the notebook (folded to 0-45 deg)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="tan_sh = Tan(alpha_sh)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>tan_sh = Tan(alpha_sh)</expbody>
      <expresult> = 0.030</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">tan alpha</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="r_sh = Min(Abs(M_2_4), Abs(M_3_4))/Max(Abs(M_2_4), Abs(M_3_4))" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>r_sh = Min(Abs(M_2_4), Abs(M_3_4))/Max(Abs(M_2_4), Abs(M_3_4))</expbody>
      <expresult> = 0.030</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">M_min / M_max of the record (equals tan alpha)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="sn_h = Sin(alpha_sh)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>sn_h = Sin(alpha_sh)</expbody>
      <expresult> = 0.030</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">sin alpha</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="cs_h = Sin(alpha_sh + (90 deg))" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>cs_h = Sin(alpha_sh + (90 deg))</expbody>
      <expresult> = 1.000</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">cos alpha</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="s_max_h = D_pile*(sn_h + cs_h)/2 to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>s_max_h = D_pile*(sn_h + cs_h)/2 to in</expbody>
      <expresult> = 9.265 in</expresult>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">centroid to the extreme compression fiber</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="s_sh_1 = -sn_h*x_st_1 + cs_h*y_st_1 to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>s_sh_1 = -sn_h*x_st_1 + cs_h*y_st_1 to in</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">strand coordinate toward the compression face</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="m_sh_1 = If(s_sh_1 &lt; -0.000000001*(1 in), 1, 0)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>m_sh_1 = If(s_sh_1 &lt; -0.000000001*(1 in), 1, 0)</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">strand on the flexural tension half depth (1)</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">
    <dynexp formula="w_sh_1 = m_sh_1*s_sh_1 to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False">
      <expbody>w_sh_1 = m_sh_1*s_sh_1 to in</expbody>
    </dynexp>
  </paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">its coordinate</paragraph>
