  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Figure 3. Demand/capacity ratio of each distilled check (stems) against the 1.0 limit. The stems are live formulas of the check ratios: a stem turns red when its ratio passes 1.0.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C" background="#F1F5FA">Check numbers: 1 local buckling D/t; 2 KL/r; 3 axial compression; 4 axial + flexure, 6.9.2.2.1; 5 shear; 6 tension; 7 pile spacing.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C" background="#F1F5FA">The notebook lists 16 PENDING items; the distilled ratios above do not close them: Local buckling class · nonslender (D/t vs 0.11 E/Fy); Slenderness KL/r ≤ 120; Axial compression · maximum Pu / φc Pn; Combined axial load and flexure · Eq. 6.9.2.2.1 (-1); Shear · round tube; Tension · maximum strength uplift; Pile Data Table completeness (SDM 11.4); Steel grade and Fy reconciled; Corrosion allowance; Environment classification; Pile-to-cap connection (12 in embedment); Downdrag source documented; FBMP export current; Minimum tip elevation; Scour resistance and elevations; Drivability.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C" background="#F1F5FA">FB-MultiPier reports a largest model D/C of 0.29 at combo 2 STRENGTH-III · pile 4 · element 13J · EL 16.55 ft. The distilled Status covers the recomputed numerical checks only; it is not design acceptance.</paragraph>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">A distilled result of ✓ covers only the recomputed numerical checks; it is not design acceptance. The pending items of the notebook stay open. Recalculate in Blockpad after any input change.</paragraph>
